// smt_encode — THE OBLIGATION WALK (1.5.0; D-218.4, D-218.6, D-218.8): one
// function instance's body, walked in program order over the SAME typed AST
// the emitter lowers, under the SAME generic bindings, producing the
// hypotheses the solver may use and the obligations it must decide. It never
// reads the IR writer -- which is what makes the obligations of the
// `--obligations` run and the `--elide` run identical by construction (P-3).
//
// THE ENCODING IS FAIL-CLOSED OPACITY (P-8). A value the walk can express is
// a term; a value it cannot is an OPAQUE symbol -- declared with its type's
// range axiom and no definition -- and the site's obligation is still recorded
// over it. Every hypothesis asserted here is a fact on every execution that
// reaches the site: a definition is the language's semantics, a range axiom
// is the type's, and the D-210/D-007 traps make the continuing path satisfy
// both. An `unsat` under those hypotheses proves the guard cannot fire on any
// continuing path. What 1.5.0 expresses: plain `intN`/`uintN` and `bool`
// values, literals, `+ - *`, `/ %` (through the truncating definitions --
// P-17), comparisons, `&& || !`, unary minus, the ternary, the widening
// cast, and a binding's definitions in straight-line code. Everything else
// is opaque, and every construct's SUBEXPRESSIONS are still walked, because
// a division inside an argument is a site whatever its parent is.
//
// NAMES ARE SOURCE-DERIVED SSA (P-5): a binding's k-th definition is
// `|name.k|`, an anonymous opaque term `|_.k|`. A branch's assignments are
// visible inside the branch and INVALIDATED after it (a fresh opaque
// version for every name either arm assigned); a loop invalidates the names
// its body assigns before the body is walked and again after it; a `defer`
// body reads every name as opaque (it runs at an exit the straight line does
// not see); and a local or parameter whose ADDRESS is taken anywhere in the
// function is never NAMED at all -- every read of it is a fresh opaque term
// (1.5.2 step 0, DEF-14). 1.5.0 gave such a name a symbol and withheld only
// its DEFINITION, but a stable symbol is itself the fact "every read is the
// same value", and a call handed the address falsifies it: `int32:a = x +
// 1i32; raw bump(@x); 100i32 / (x - a)` kept `|a.1| = |x.1| + 1` across the
// call, z3 proved the divisor -1, and the elided build divided by zero where
// the plain build reached `failsafe`. Contracts as hypotheses are 1.5.3's.
//
// PATH CONDITIONS (1.5.4 step 1; L-1..L-6 in meta/roadmap/1.5/1.5.4.md): a
// branch condition is a fact INSIDE the arm it guards and its negation a fact
// where the arm cannot have been taken -- an `if`'s condition in its then-arm
// and `(not c)` in its else-arm; a `pick` arm's pattern (`(= sel v)`, a
// range) and the negations of the arms before it, its `where` guard once
// inside; after an arm that never falls through (a syntactic terminator:
// `pass`, `fail`, `return`, `exit`, `trap`, `break`, `continue`, `give`, and
// blocks, `if`s and `pick`s made only of those) the OTHER arm's condition
// holds; after a loop nothing `break`s out of, its condition is false; a
// `when`'s `then` block knows the condition held at the first head visit and
// its `end` block that it did not and that the loop changed nothing. Each is
// pushed in the region it is a fact of, so the cone's dominance rule keeps it
// where it belongs.
//
// THE MERGE (1.5.4 step 2; L-7..L-10): a region opened for an ARM carries its
// condition, and leaving it re-pushes every hypothesis recorded directly in
// it into the parent as `(=> c H)` -- a fact of an arm is a fact after the
// arm under the arm's condition (an execution past the arm with `c` true
// fell through the arm's straight line and so passed every site of it; with
// `c` false the implication is vacuous). A loop body's hypotheses are one
// symbolic iteration's and are never re-pushed; a `defer`'s neither. On that
// footing the versions after an `if`, a `when` or a `pick` MERGE: a binding
// the arms left at different versions gets a new one defined `(ite c_1 v_1
// (ite c_2 v_2 ... v_n))` over the arms that fall through, and a havoc only
// where an arm has no condition term or an unnamed version. A pick
// expression's value is the same chain over its arms' `give` terms. `&&`,
// `||` and the ternary are arms too: the right-hand side and the two branches
// are encoded in regions of their own under `a`, `(not a)`, `c`, `(not c)`.
//
// THE COUNTERS (1.5.4 step 3; L-11..L-14): a counted loop's `$` and a range
// `for`'s binding are TERMS. The bounds and the step are captured at entry
// (fresh symbols equal to their terms, as the emitter's slots are -- D-234's
// rule), the direction is `asc = start < limit` as the emitter computes it
// once; the ENTRY row sees the counter at its start; in the body it is a
// fresh symbol inside its range (`start <= $ < limit` ascending, `limit < $
// <= start` descending, and on a numeral step in the right residue class);
// the PRESERVATION and `continue` rows see the incremented counter the head
// will see; after a loop nothing `break`s out of, the invariant holds over
// the EXIT value (past the limit by less than a numeral step; a range's
// binding exactly at its bound). A computed step's positivity is the
// `loop-step` row (S-46), its compare the guard; a literal step is the
// checker's and has neither.
//
// THE CONE (P-4): an obligation's canonical text is the relevance closure of
// its goal over the hypotheses that DOMINATE it -- recorded before it, in a
// branch region on the path from the function's entry to the site. Later
// definitions describe values that exist only if execution passes later
// traps, and a sibling branch's definitions describe values the site's path
// never computes (a then-arm's `x.2 = x.1 + 1`, in range by D-210's trap,
// would otherwise tell an else-arm site that `x.1 < MAX`); using either
// would be unsound. Its SHA-256 over (text, symbol, kind) is the
// obligation's identity (D-218.8).

mod:smt_encode;

use "../../frontend/intern.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/token_kind.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/source_location.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/ast_kind.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/ast.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/parse_expr.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/parse_stmt.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/parse_decl.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/parse_decorate.npk".*;   // limit_target (1.5.2 step 2, D-251)
use "../../frontend/parse_pick.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/types.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/expr_types.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/symbols.npk".*;   // a free call's callee, by its symbol (1.5.2 step 3)
use "../../frontend/type_resolve.npk".*;
use "../../../lib/nhash.npk".*;
use "../ir/ir_types.npk".*;
use "./smt_writer.npk".*;
use "./smt_kinds.npk".*;

// --- the state -----------------------------------------------------------------------

// A declared constant.
pub struct:SmtSym = {
    string:text;      // `|x.2|`
    bool:is_bool;     // Bool, else Int
    // AN UNINTERPRETED FUNCTION (1.5.3 step 2, L-3): a `pure never fails`
    // callee's symbol, declared `(declare-fun |f| <sorts> <sort>)` -- its
    // argument sorts as one text, "" for a constant.
    string:sorts;
};

// One hypothesis: its text and the symbols it mentions (by index into `syms`).
pub struct:SmtHyp = {
    string:text;
    List<int32>:syms;
    int32:region;            // the branch region it was recorded in
};

// One obligation, as the walk records it; `finish` fills the cone and the hash.
pub struct:SmtObl = {
    int32:kind;
    string:goal;             // the property to prove (the file asserts its negation)
    List<int32>:syms;        // the goal's symbols
    int64:hyps;              // hypotheses recorded before it: the cone draws from [0, hyps)
    int32:site;              // the node index that identifies the site (the emitter's key) ...
    int32:space;             // ... in this id space (L-9): SITE_EXPR, SITE_STMT or SITE_DECL
    int32:ordinal;           // the k-th of its kind in this function
    int32:ctx;               // the clause context the site was recorded under (1.5.3 step 2; `LlCtx.cur_ctx`)
    int32:role;              // ROLE_* (1.5.3 step 2, L-13): what the row's retention keeps
    int32:group;             // the rows one guard shares (a loop's three rows, a call's bypass rows)
    int32:traps;             // the traps the group keeps when any of its rows is retained
    int32:line;
    int32:col;
    int32:region;            // the branch region of the site
    bool:encoded;            // false: an `unencoded` row (P-12)
    List<int32>:cone_syms;   // filled by finish: symbols in the cone, ascending
    List<int32>:cone_hyps;   // filled by finish: hypotheses in the cone, in order
    string:canon;            // filled by finish: the canonical text
    string:hash;             // filled by finish: sha256 hex of canon + symbol + kind
    bool:discharged;         // set by the elision reader: the manifest says so
};

// A binding in scope: the name, its current symbol (-1: none -- reads of it
// are opaque), and its type.
struct:Bind = {
    int32:name;
    int32:sym;
    int32:type_id;
    int32:rule;      // the `Rules` declaration limiting the name (1.5.2, D-251); 0 for none
    int32:entry;     // the binding's FIRST version (1.5.3 step 2, D-243): what `old(...)` reads
};

// A term: encodable or not; when encodable, its text, sort and symbols.
struct:Term = {
    bool:ok;
    bool:is_bool;
    string:text;
    List<int32>:syms;
};

pub struct:Encoder = {
    Ast->:ast;
    ExprTypes->:et;
    SymbolTable->:tab;         // a free call's callee is its identifier's symbol (1.5.2 step 3)
    TypeTable->:types;
    InternTable->:interns;
    LlCtx->:ctx;
    TypeResolver->:tr;
    int32:scope;
    string:symbol;             // the function instance's mangled symbol
    List<SmtSym>:syms;
    List<SmtHyp>:hyps;
    List<SmtObl>:obls;
    List<Bind>:binds;
    List<int32>:ver_name;      // per-name version counters
    List<int32>:ver_next;
    List<int32>:escaped;       // names whose address is taken: never defined
    int32:anon;                // anonymous opaque counter
    List<int32>:ordinals;      // per-kind ordinal counters, OK_COUNT + 1 slots
    bool:nonlinear;            // a non-literal `*` or a non-literal divisor appeared
    bool:uses_sdiv;            // a signed division term appeared (the define-funs are needed)
    List<int32>:region_parent; // branch regions: each one's parent (the root's is -1)
    int32:cur_region;          // the region the walk is in
    // A REGION'S CONDITION AND ITS FIRST HYPOTHESIS (1.5.4 step 2, L-7):
    // `term_none` for a region that is not an arm (a loop body, a `defer`,
    // a pick arm without a pattern term); the hypothesis index the region
    // began at, so leaving it can re-push what it recorded, guarded.
    List<Term>:region_cond;
    List<int64>:region_hyp0;
    // THE LAST `give` WALKED (L-9): a pick expression's arm ends in one, and
    // the arm's value is its term.
    Term:last_give;
    // THE COUNTERS (1.5.4 step 3, L-11): `$` of every enclosing counted
    // loop, innermost last -- the term `$` reads outside a rule -- and, per
    // loop frame, the counter's kind (0 none, 1 a range `for` binding, 2
    // `$`), the binding's name, its step and direction terms, and the index
    // of its `$` entry in `dollars`, so a `continue` can see the incremented
    // counter of the loop it re-enters.
    List<Term>:dollars;
    List<int32>:loop_ckind;
    List<int32>:loop_cname;
    List<Term>:loop_cstep;
    List<Term>:loop_casc;
    List<int64>:loop_cdollar;
    // THE RULE'S SUBJECT (1.5.2 step 3, L-8): the term `$` stands for while a
    // `Rules` body is being instantiated by `enc_rule`; `term_none` outside.
    Term:subject;
    // QUIET (1.5.2 step 3): nonzero while `enc_rule` encodes a rule's clauses,
    // so a guard site INSIDE a clause -- a division -- records no row of the
    // instantiating function's: the guard is the predicate function's own,
    // and the row is recorded there, once (L-1).
    int32:quiet;
    // THE CONTRACTS' STATE (1.5.3 step 2): `result` while an `ensures` is
    // encoded (`term_none` outside one); `at_entry` while an `old(...)`
    // operand is encoded, so a name reads its entry version; the function's
    // declaration, its impl and its trait (0 outside a method), its success
    // type, and whether it is `failsafe`; the clause context a row is
    // recorded under (0 outside a clause); and the loop stack a `continue`
    // resolves against -- each loop's statement, label and invariant.
    Term:result;
    bool:at_entry;
    int32:fn_decl;
    int32:impl_decl;
    int32:trait_ty;
    int32:ret_type;
    bool:is_failsafe;
    int32:clause_ctx;
    List<int32>:loop_sids;
    List<int32>:loop_labels;
    List<int32>:loop_invs;
};

// Branch regions (the dominance rule): a then-arm, an else-arm, a loop body,
// a pick arm, a `when` block and a `defer` body each open a child region of
// the one they sit in; straight-line blocks stay in their region.
func:region_enter = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    drop region_enter_cond(e, raw term_none());
    pass NIL;
};

// AN ARM'S REGION (1.5.4 step 2, L-7): it carries the condition under which
// its facts hold after it, and the hypothesis index it began at.
func:region_enter_cond = NIL(Encoder->:e, Term:c) never fails {
    drop list_push(@e.region_parent, e.cur_region);
    drop list_push(@e.region_cond, raw term_copy(c));
    drop list_push(@e.region_hyp0, e.hyps.count);
    e.cur_region = (e.region_parent.count - 1i64) =>! int32;
    pass NIL;
};

// LEAVING AN ARM RE-PUSHES ITS FACTS, GUARDED (L-7): every hypothesis
// recorded DIRECTLY in the region since it began -- a definition, a range
// axiom, a rule, a callee's `ensures`, an inner arm's already-guarded copies
// -- goes into the parent as `(=> c H)`. The arm's own condition is not
// re-pushed (`(=> c c)` says nothing). A region without a condition
// re-pushes nothing: a loop body's facts are one iteration's, a `defer`'s
// run at an exit the straight line does not see.
func:region_leave = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    int32:r = e.cur_region;
    int32:parent = e.region_parent.items[r => int64];
    if (e.region_cond.items[r => int64].ok) {
        Term:c = raw term_copy(e.region_cond.items[r => int64]);
        int64:n0 = e.hyps.count;
        for (int64:h in e.region_hyp0.items[r => int64]...n0) {
            if (e.hyps.items[h].region != r) { continue; }
            if (string_equals(e.hyps.items[h].text, c.text)) { continue; }
            string:gt = raw smt_app2("=>", c.text, e.hyps.items[h].text);
            List<int32>:gs = raw syms_union(c.syms, e.hyps.items[h].syms);
            drop hyp_push_in(e, gt, gs, parent);
        }
    }
    e.cur_region = parent;
    pass NIL;
};

// Is region `h` on the path from the root to region `o`?
func:region_dominates = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:h, int32:o) never fails {
    int32:r = o;
    int32:fuel = 4096i32;
    while ((r >= 0i32) && (fuel > 0i32)) {
        if (r == h) { pass true; }
        r = e.region_parent.items[r => int64];
        fuel = fuel - 1i32;
    }
    pass false;
};

pub func:enc_init = Encoder(Ast->:ast, ExprTypes->:et, SymbolTable->:tab, TypeTable->:types,
                            InternTable->:interns, LlCtx->:ctx, TypeResolver->:tr,
                            int32:scope, string:symbol) never fails {
    List<int32>:ords = raw list_init::<int32>(((raw OK_COUNT()) => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...(((raw OK_COUNT()) => int64) + 1i64)) { drop list_push(@ords, 0i32); }
    List<int32>:rp = raw list_init::<int32>(8i64);
    drop list_push(@rp, 0i32 - 1i32);   // the root region
    List<Term>:rc = raw list_init::<Term>(8i64);
    drop list_push(@rc, raw term_none());
    List<int64>:rh = raw list_init::<int64>(8i64);
    drop list_push(@rh, 0i64);
    pass Encoder{ ast: ast, et: et, tab: tab, types: types, interns: interns, ctx: ctx, tr: tr,
                  scope: scope, symbol: string_concat(symbol, ""),
                  syms: raw list_init::<SmtSym>(32i64),
                  hyps: raw list_init::<SmtHyp>(32i64),
                  obls: raw list_init::<SmtObl>(8i64),
                  binds: raw list_init::<Bind>(16i64),
                  ver_name: raw list_init::<int32>(16i64),
                  ver_next: raw list_init::<int32>(16i64),
                  escaped: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  anon: 0i32, ordinals: move(ords), nonlinear: false, uses_sdiv: false,
                  region_parent: move(rp), cur_region: 0i32,
                  region_cond: move(rc), region_hyp0: move(rh), last_give: raw term_none(),
                  dollars: raw list_init::<Term>(4i64),
                  loop_ckind: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  loop_cname: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  loop_cstep: raw list_init::<Term>(4i64),
                  loop_casc: raw list_init::<Term>(4i64),
                  loop_cdollar: raw list_init::<int64>(4i64),
                  subject: raw term_none(), quiet: 0i32,
                  result: raw term_none(), at_entry: false, fn_decl: 0i32, impl_decl: 0i32,
                  trait_ty: 0i32, ret_type: 0i32, is_failsafe: false, clause_ctx: 0i32,
                  loop_sids: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  loop_labels: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  loop_invs: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64) };
};

// --- types -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

// An expression's recorded type, under the instance's binding.
func:ty_of = int32(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    pass (raw subst_emitted_param(e.ctx, raw exprtypes_get(e.et, id)));
};

func:is_int = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ty == 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_INT()));
};

func:is_bool = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ty == 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_BOOL()));
};

// --- symbols and hypotheses --------------------------------------------------------------

func:hyp_push = NIL(Encoder->:e, string:text, List<int32>:syms) never fails {
    drop hyp_push_in(e, text, syms, e.cur_region);
    pass NIL;
};

// A hypothesis in a NAMED region (1.5.4 step 2): the guarded re-push writes
// into the parent of the region it is leaving.
func:hyp_push_in = NIL(Encoder->:e, string:text, List<int32>:syms, int32:region) never fails {
    List<int32>:copy = raw list_init::<int32>(syms.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...syms.count) { drop list_push(@copy, syms.items[i]); }
    SmtHyp:h = SmtHyp{ text: string_concat(text, ""), syms: move(copy), region: region };
    drop list_push(@e.hyps, move(h));
    pass NIL;
};

// Declare a constant; an integer one gets its range axiom as a hypothesis.
func:sym_new = int32(Encoder->:e, string:text, int32:ty) never fails {
    bool:b = raw is_bool(e, ty);
    SmtSym:s = SmtSym{ text: string_concat(text, ""), is_bool: b, sorts: "" };
    drop list_push(@e.syms, move(s));
    int32:idx = (e.syms.count - 1i64) =>! int32;
    if (raw is_int(e, ty)) {
        List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop list_push(@one, idx);
        drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_range_axiom(text, raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty),
                                              raw type_is_signed(e.types, ty)), one);
    }
    pass idx;
};

func:sym_text = string(Encoder->:e, int32:idx) never fails {
    pass (string_concat(e.syms.items[idx => int64].text, ""));
};

// A declared symbol by its text, or -1.
func:sym_find = int32(Encoder->:e, string:text) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.syms.count) {
        if (string_equals(e.syms.items[i].text, text)) { pass (i =>! int32); }
    }
    pass 0i32 - 1i32;
};

// AN UNINTERPRETED FUNCTION SYMBOL (1.5.3 step 2, L-3): declared once per
// text, with its argument sorts and its result sort; a function symbol rides
// in a term's symbol list like a constant, so the cone closure declares it
// where an application appears.
func:sym_new_fun = int32(Encoder->:e, string:text, string:sorts, bool:ret_bool) never fails {
    int32:have = raw sym_find(e, text);
    if (have >= 0i32) { pass have; }
    SmtSym:s = SmtSym{ text: string_concat(text, ""), is_bool: ret_bool,
                       sorts: string_concat(sorts, "") };
    drop list_push(@e.syms, move(s));
    pass ((e.syms.count - 1i64) =>! int32);
};

// A fresh anonymous opaque symbol of an int or bool type, as a term.
func:term_opaque = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (!((raw is_int(e, ty)) || (raw is_bool(e, ty)))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    e.anon = e.anon + 1i32;
    string:nm = raw smt_sym("_", e.anon => int64);
    int32:idx = raw sym_new(e, nm, ty);
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, idx);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: raw is_bool(e, ty), text: move(nm), syms: move(one) };
};

func:term_none = Term() never fails {
    pass Term{ ok: false, is_bool: false, text: "", syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64) };
};

func:term_lit = Term(string:text, bool:is_bool) never fails {
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: is_bool, text: string_concat(text, ""),
               syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64) };
};

func:syms_union = List<int32>(List<int32>:a, List<int32>:b) never fails {
    List<int32>:out = raw list_init::<int32>(a.count + b.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...a.count) { drop list_push(@out, a.items[i]); }
    for (int64:j in 0i64...b.count) {
        bool:have = false;
        for (int64:k in 0i64...out.count) { if (out.items[k] == b.items[j]) { have = true; } }
        if (!have) { drop list_push(@out, b.items[j]); }
    }
    pass out;
};

func:term_app2 = Term(string:op, Term:a, Term:b, bool:is_bool) never fails {
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: is_bool, text: raw smt_app2(op, a.text, b.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(a.syms, b.syms) };
};

// Is the term a plain numeral (so a product or a division by it is linear)?
func:term_is_numeral = bool(Term:t) never fails {
    if (!t.ok) { pass false; }
    if (t.text.len == 0i64) { pass false; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...t.text.len) {
        uint8:c = t.text.ptr[i];
        if ((c < 48u8) || (c > 57u8)) { pass false; }
    }
    pass true;
};

// --- bindings and versions ---------------------------------------------------------------

func:version_next = int64(Encoder->:e, int32:name) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.ver_name.count) {
        if (e.ver_name.items[i] == name) {
            int32:k = e.ver_next.items[i];
            e.ver_next.items[i] = k + 1i32;
            pass (k => int64);
        }
    }
    drop list_push(@e.ver_name, name);
    drop list_push(@e.ver_next, 2i32);
    pass 1i64;
};

func:bind_find = int64(Encoder->:e, int32:name) never fails {
    int64:i = e.binds.count;
    while (i > 0i64) {
        i = i - 1i64;
        if (e.binds.items[i].name == name) { pass i; }
    }
    pass (0i64 - 1i64);
};

func:is_escaped = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:name) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.escaped.count) { if (e.escaped.items[i] == name) { pass true; } }
    pass false;
};

// A new version of `name` with type `ty`: defined by `t` when the type is
// int/bool and the term is encodable; opaque (range axiom only) when the
// term is not; symbol-less when the type is neither -- or when the name is
// ADDRESS-TAKEN (DEF-14: an escaped name is never named, so every read of it
// is a fresh opaque term and no fact about it can outlive a call). A
// SUBSTITUTION binding (`enc_under`: a callee's parameter bound to an
// argument term already computed) never consults the escaped set -- the set
// is the CALLER's names, and a callee parameter that happened to share one
// bound unnamed and left its call-site row `open` (DEF-27, 1.5.4 step 0).
func:bind_define = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, int32:ty, Term:t, int32:rule,
                       bool:substitution) never fails {
    int32:sym = 0i32 - 1i32;
    bool:named = (raw is_int(e, ty)) || (raw is_bool(e, ty));
    if ((!substitution) && (raw is_escaped(e, name))) { named = false; }
    if (named) {
        string:nm = raw smt_sym(raw intern_get(e.interns, name), raw version_next(e, name));
        sym = raw sym_new(e, nm, ty);
        bool:define = t.ok;
        if (define) {
            if (t.is_bool != (raw is_bool(e, ty))) { define = false; }
        }
        if (define) {
            List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop list_push(@one, sym);
            drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", nm, t.text), raw syms_union(one, t.syms));
        }
    }
    Bind:b = Bind{ name: name, sym: sym, type_id: ty, rule: rule, entry: sym };
    drop list_push(@e.binds, move(b));
    pass NIL;
};

// Assignment to an existing binding: a new version in place (same type). An
// escaped name stays unnamed (DEF-14).
func:bind_assign = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, Term:t) never fails {
    int64:i = raw bind_find(e, name);
    if (i < 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    int32:ty = e.binds.items[i].type_id;
    if (!((raw is_int(e, ty)) || (raw is_bool(e, ty)))) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw is_escaped(e, name)) { pass NIL; }
    string:nm = raw smt_sym(raw intern_get(e.interns, name), raw version_next(e, name));
    int32:sym = raw sym_new(e, nm, ty);
    bool:define = t.ok;
    if (define) { if (t.is_bool != (raw is_bool(e, ty))) { define = false; } }
    if (define) {
        List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop list_push(@one, sym);
        drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", nm, t.text), raw syms_union(one, t.syms));
    }
    e.binds.items[i].sym = sym;
    pass NIL;
};

// Every binding named in `names` gets a fresh OPAQUE version (the value after a
// construct the straight line does not see through). An escaped name has no
// version to refresh (DEF-14).
func:invalidate = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<int32>:names) never fails {
    for (int64:k in 0i64...names.count) {
        int64:i = raw bind_find(e, names.items[k]);
        if (i < 0i64) { continue; }
        int32:ty = e.binds.items[i].type_id;
        if (!((raw is_int(e, ty)) || (raw is_bool(e, ty)))) { continue; }
        if (raw is_escaped(e, names.items[k])) { continue; }
        string:nm = raw smt_sym(raw intern_get(e.interns, names.items[k]),
                                raw version_next(e, names.items[k]));
        e.binds.items[i].sym = raw sym_new(e, nm, ty);
        // A LIMITED NAME KEEPS ITS RULE ACROSS A MERGE (L-7): the fresh
        // version is "the value after the construct", and every write inside
        // was guarded by the rule -- the hypothesis, no obligation.
        drop assert_rule(e, i);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:invalidate_all = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    List<int32>:names = raw list_init::<int32>(e.binds.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.binds.count) { drop list_push(@names, e.binds.items[i].name); }
    drop invalidate(e, names);
    pass NIL;
};

// The symbols of every binding, to restore after a branch.
func:snapshot = List<int32>(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    List<int32>:out = raw list_init::<int32>(e.binds.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.binds.count) { drop list_push(@out, e.binds.items[i].sym); }
    pass out;
};

func:restore = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<int32>:snap) never fails {
    int64:n = snap.count;
    if (e.binds.count < n) { n = e.binds.count; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...n) { e.binds.items[i].sym = snap.items[i]; }
    pass NIL;
};

func:scope_mark = int64(Encoder->:e) never fails { pass e.binds.count; };
func:scope_release = NIL(Encoder->:e, int64:mark) never fails { e.binds.count = mark; pass NIL; };

// --- obligations ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

func:record = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:kind, string:goal, List<int32>:syms, int32:space,
                  int32:site, Span:at, bool:encoded) never fails {
    drop record_at(e, kind, goal, syms, space, site, at, encoded, raw ROLE_GUARD(), site, 1i32);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE FULL ROW (1.5.3 step 2, L-13): its role, the group it shares a guard
// with, and the traps that guard keeps when any row of the group is
// retained -- what the runners' belts read from `rows.txt`.
func:record_at = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:kind, string:goal, List<int32>:syms, int32:space,
                     int32:site, Span:at, bool:encoded, int32:role, int32:group,
                     int32:traps) never fails {
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:ord = e.ordinals.items[kind => int64] + 1i32;
    e.ordinals.items[kind => int64] = ord;
    List<int32>:copy = raw list_init::<int32>(syms.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...syms.count) { drop list_push(@copy, syms.items[i]); }
    SmtObl:o = SmtObl{ kind: kind, goal: string_concat(goal, ""), syms: move(copy),
                       hyps: e.hyps.count, site: site, space: space, ordinal: ord,
                       ctx: e.clause_ctx, role: role, group: group, traps: traps,
                       line: at.line, col: at.col, region: e.cur_region, encoded: encoded,
                       cone_syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       cone_hyps: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       canon: "", hash: "", discharged: false };
    drop list_push(@e.obls, move(o));
    pass NIL;
};

// The D-007 pair at a plain-integer division: `b != 0`, and for a signed
// width `not (a == MIN and b == -1)`. Terms that could not be expressed are
// stood in for by opaque symbols, so the obligation is recorded whatever the
// operands were (P-8, P-12).
func:record_division = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:lt, Term:a, Term:b, int32:site,
                           Span:at) never fails {
    Term:ta = raw term_copy(a);
    Term:tb = raw term_copy(b);
    if (!ta.ok) { ta = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
    if (!tb.ok) { tb = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
    string:zero = raw smt_app1("not", raw smt_app2("=", tb.text, "0"));
    drop record(e, raw OK_DIV_ZERO(), zero, tb.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, lt)) {
        string:mn = raw smt_int_min(raw type_int_bits(e.types, lt));
        string:both = raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2("=", ta.text, mn),
                                   raw smt_app2("=", tb.text, "(- 1)"));
        drop record(e, raw OK_DIV_MIN(), raw smt_app1("not", both),
                    raw syms_union(ta.syms, tb.syms), raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A `limit` write point whose rule the encoder does not yet express (1.5.2
// step 2; P-12): the row exists from the first commit that emits the guard,
// so the manifest stays an inventory of guards; step 3 give_terms it a goal.
func:record_limit_unencoded = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:space, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop record(e, raw OK_LIMIT(), "", none, space, site, at, false);
    pass NIL;
};

// The `Rules` declaration a limit node resolved to, as an index; 0 for none.
func:limit_rule_of = int32(Encoder->:e, VerifyId:v) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(v)) { pass 0i32; }
    pass ((raw limit_target(raw ast_verify(e.ast, v))).index);
};

// The NAME of the local a place is rooted at (1.5.2 step 2, D-251), or 0:
// through member and index bases whose type is not a pointer, slice or
// handle (that storage is not the binding's own) to the identifier -- the
// emitter's `place_root_local`, in the walk's terms.
func:limited_root_name = int32(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = id;
    int32:fuel = 64i32;
    while (fuel > 0i32) {
        fuel = fuel - 1i32;
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass 0i32; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, cur);
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, n.payload =>! int32);
            if (bi < 0i64) { pass 0i32; }
            pass n.payload =>! int32;
        }
        ExprId:base = ExprId{ index: 0i32 };
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
            base = raw expr_operand(n);
        } else {
            if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
                base = raw expr_lhs(n);
            } else {
                pass 0i32;
            }
        }
        int32:bt = raw ty_of(e, base);
        if (bt != 0i32) {
            int32:bk = raw type_kind(e.types, bt);
            if (bk == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass 0i32; }
            if (bk == (raw TY_SLICE()))   { pass 0i32; }
            if (bk == (raw TY_HANDLE()))  { pass 0i32; }
        }
        cur = base;
    }
    pass 0i32;
};

// A binding's current version as a term; `term_none` when it has no symbol
// (an address-taken name, or a type outside the fragment).
func:bind_term = Term(Encoder->:e, int64:bi) never fails {
    int32:sym = e.binds.items[bi].sym;
    if (sym < 0i32) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, sym);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: e.syms.items[sym => int64].is_bool,
               text: raw sym_text(e, sym), syms: move(one) };
};

// A CLAUSE THE ENCODER CANNOT EXPRESS (L-8): a fresh opaque Bool named for
// the rule and the clause (`|r_call.c1.7|`, P-5's shape with the anonymous
// counter as k). As a goal conjunct it makes the row `open`; as a hypothesis
// it asserts nothing usable -- fail-closed either way (P-8).
func:clause_opaque = Term(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d, int32:j) never fails {
    e.anon = e.anon + 1i32;
    string:base = string_concat(raw intern_get(e.interns, raw decl_name(d)), ".c");
    base = string_concat(base, int_to_string((j + 1i32) => int64));
    string:nm = raw smt_sym(base, e.anon => int64);
    int32:idx = raw sym_new(e, nm, e.types.t_bool);
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, idx);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: move(nm), syms: move(one) };
};

// THE RULE OVER A TERM (1.5.2 step 3, L-8): the conjunction, in source order,
// of every refinement's rule (recursively -- resolve refused cycles,
// RESOLVE-006; the fuel is a belt) and every clause encoded with `$` bound
// to the subject. `term_none` only when the SUBJECT has no term (a type
// outside the fragment); an inexpressible clause is an opaque conjunct. The
// clauses are encoded QUIET: a guard inside one is the predicate function's
// own site and is recorded there (L-1), never here.
func:enc_rule = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:rule, Term:subject, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (!subject.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: rule });
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclRuleDecl) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    Term:acc = raw term_none();
    bool:first = true;
    int32:rn = raw rule_refine_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...rn) {
        VerifyNode:rv = raw ast_verify(e.ast, raw rule_refine(e.ast, d, i));
        Term:sub = raw enc_rule(e, (raw limit_target(rv)).index, raw term_copy(subject), fuel - 1i32);
        if (!sub.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (first) { acc = move(sub); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, sub, true); }
    }
    int32:cn = raw rule_clause_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:j in 0i32...cn) {
        Term:saved = raw term_copy(e.subject);
        e.subject = raw term_copy(subject);
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:c = raw enc_expr(e, raw rule_clause(e.ast, d, j));
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        e.subject = move(saved);
        if (!(c.ok && c.is_bool)) { c = raw clause_opaque(e, d, j); }
        if (first) { acc = move(c); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, c, true); }
    }
    if (first) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
    pass acc;
};

// THE RULE AS A HYPOTHESIS on a binding's current version (L-7): pushed
// after a write point's own obligation (so the goal is never in its own
// cone) and at every invalidation. Sound because every write to the binding
// is guarded by this rule or discharged under these same hypotheses (P-8).
func:assert_rule = NIL(Encoder->:e, int64:bi) never fails {
    int32:rule = e.binds.items[bi].rule;
    if (rule == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:v = raw bind_term(e, bi);
    if (!v.ok) { pass NIL; }
    Term:r = raw enc_rule(e, rule, v, 64i32);
    if (!r.ok) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, r.text, r.syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// A `limit` ROW at a write point of binding `bi`: the rule over the new
// version, encoded; `unencoded` when the version has no term (L-6).
func:record_limit = NIL(Encoder->:e, int64:bi, int32:space, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    int32:rule = e.binds.items[bi].rule;
    if (rule == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:v = raw bind_term(e, bi);
    if (!v.ok) { drop record_limit_unencoded(e, space, site, at); pass NIL; }
    Term:g = raw enc_rule(e, rule, v, 64i32);
    if (!g.ok) { drop record_limit_unencoded(e, space, site, at); pass NIL; }
    drop record(e, raw OK_LIMIT(), g.text, g.syms, space, site, at, true);
    pass NIL;
};

// AFTER A WRITE to `name` (L-7's order): the site's obligation, then the rule
// as a hypothesis. Nothing for an unlimited or unbound name.
func:after_write = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, int32:space, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    if (name == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, name);
    if (bi < 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    if (e.binds.items[bi].rule == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop record_limit(e, bi, space, site, at);
    drop assert_rule(e, bi);
    pass NIL;
};

// A CALL, ENCODED ONCE (1.5.2 step 3, L-10; 1.5.3 step 2): the receiver or
// callee expression and every argument (their sites recorded, their terms
// kept), and the callee the checker recorded -- a method call's declaration
// (`exprtypes_set_callee`), a free call's identifier's symbol as `emit_call`
// resolves it; a local or parameter holding a function value is an indirect
// call and has no rows (its entry check covers it). `terms`/`types`/`names`
// are per PARAMETER position: the receiver is parameter 0 when the method
// takes one more parameter than the call passes arguments.
struct:CallEnc = {
    int32:cd;              // the callee's declaration, 0 for none usable
    bool:coroutine;        // `async` or `thread`: the entry check runs at state 0, never bypassed
    bool:through_dyn;      // the receiver is a `dyn`: the vtable's target is the entry, never bypassed
    List<int32>:names;
    List<int32>:types;
    List<Term>:terms;
};

func:enc_call = CallEnc(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    Term:rcv = raw term_none();
    int32:rty = 0i32;
    if (n.a != 0i32) {
        rcv = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        rty = raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
    }
    int32:g = 0i32;
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) { g = raw expr_generic_count(n); }
    int32:argc = n.c - g;
    List<Term>:args = raw list_init::<Term>((argc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<int32>:atys = raw list_init::<int32>((argc => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...argc) {
        ExprId:aid = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, g + i) };
        drop list_push(@args, raw enc_expr(e, aid));
        drop list_push(@atys, raw ty_of(e, aid));
    }
    CallEnc:none = CallEnc{ cd: 0i32, coroutine: false, through_dyn: false,
                            names: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64), types: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                            terms: raw list_init::<Term>(1i64) };
    int32:cd = raw exprtypes_callee(e.et, id);
    if ((cd == 0i32) && (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) && (n.a != 0i32)) {
        ExprNode:cn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        if ((cn.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) && (cn.a != 0i32)) {
            Symbol:cs = raw symtab_get(e.tab, cn.a);
            if (cs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) { cd = cs.origin; }
        }
    }
    if (cd == 0i32) { pass none; }
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: cd });
    if (cdn.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass none; }
    if (!(raw decl_is_none(raw fn_variadic(e.ast, cdn)))) { pass none; }
    int32:pc = raw fn_param_count(e.ast, cdn);
    int32:off = 0i32;
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) {
        if (pc == (argc + 1i32)) { off = 1i32; }
        else { if (pc != argc) { pass none; } }
    } else {
        if (pc != argc) { pass none; }
    }
    List<int32>:names = raw list_init::<int32>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<int32>:types = raw list_init::<int32>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<Term>:terms = raw list_init::<Term>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int32:p in 0i32...pc) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(e.ast, raw fn_param(e.ast, cdn, p));
        drop list_push(@names, raw decl_name(pd));
        if ((off == 1i32) && (p == 0i32)) {
            drop list_push(@types, rty);
            drop list_push(@terms, raw term_copy(rcv));
        } else {
            int64:ai = (p - off) => int64;
            drop list_push(@types, atys.items[ai]);
            drop list_push(@terms, raw term_copy(args.items[ai]));
        }
    }
    bool:co = (raw decl_has(cdn, raw DECL_ASYNC())) || (raw decl_has(cdn, raw DECL_THREAD()));
    bool:dy = false;
    if (rty != 0i32) { if ((raw type_kind(e.types, rty)) == (raw TY_DYN())) { dy = true; } }
    pass CallEnc{ cd: cd, coroutine: co, through_dyn: dy, names: move(names),
                  types: move(types), terms: move(terms) };
};

// The two call-site rows of a recorded callee (L-10, D-268): its role is
// `bypass` at a direct sync call -- discharged with every other bypass row of
// the call, the call names the body -- and `held` at an `await` or through a
// `dyn`, where the guard is the callee's own entry and no build can remove it.
func:record_call_rows = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n, CallEnc:ce) never fails {
    if (ce.cd == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:role = raw ROLE_BYPASS();
    if (ce.coroutine || ce.through_dyn) { role = raw ROLE_HELD(); }
    drop record_subsume_ce(e, id, n, ce, role);
    drop record_requires(e, id, n, ce, role);
    pass NIL;
};

// A CALL's `limit-subsume` ROW (L-10): for a callee whose declaration has
// limited parameters, ONE row per call site -- the conjunction over those
// parameters of their rules over the argument terms, with the caller's cone
// as the hypotheses (a limited-binding argument brings its rule: the spec's
// "one `Rules` implies another at a boundary"). An argument the encoder
// cannot name is opaque (the row is `open`); one whose type is outside the
// fragment makes the row `unencoded`. A `dyn` call's trait method has no
// limited parameter (TYPE-064), and a coroutine callee's row is `held`
// (D-268 amending D-252): recorded, never elided.
func:record_subsume_ce = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n, CallEnc:ce, int32:role) never fails {
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: ce.cd });
    int32:pc = raw fn_param_count(e.ast, cdn);
    Term:acc = raw term_none();
    bool:first = true;
    bool:has_limited = false;
    bool:broken = false;
    for (int32:i2 in 0i32...pc) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(e.ast, raw fn_param(e.ast, cdn, i2));
        VerifyId:pl = raw param_limit(pd);
        if (raw verify_is_none(pl)) { continue; }
        has_limited = true;
        int32:rule = (raw limit_target(raw ast_verify(e.ast, pl))).index;
        Term:a = raw term_copy(ce.terms.items[i2 => int64]);
        if (!a.ok) { a = raw term_opaque(e, ce.types.items[i2 => int64]); }
        if (!a.ok) { broken = true; continue; }
        Term:c = raw enc_rule(e, rule, a, 64i32);
        if (!c.ok) { broken = true; continue; }
        if (first) { acc = move(c); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, c, true); }
    }
    if (!has_limited) { pass NIL; }
    if (broken) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record_at(e, raw OK_LIMIT_SUBSUME(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, false,
                       role, id.index, 0i32);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop record_at(e, raw OK_LIMIT_SUBSUME(), acc.text, acc.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, true,
                   role, id.index, 0i32);
    pass NIL;
};

// A CALL's `requires` ROW (1.5.3 step 2; L-7, D-268): the callee's clauses
// conjoined over the argument terms -- the parameters bound to them by
// position (the receiver first), QUIET, since a guard inside a clause is
// the callee's own (L-5). ONE row per call, whatever the callee's kind: the
// only place the call is ever proven.
func:record_requires = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n, CallEnc:ce, int32:role) never fails {
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: ce.cd });
    if ((raw contract_count(e, cdn, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES())) == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:g = raw enc_under(e, ce.names, ce.types, ce.terms, cdn, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), false,
                           raw term_none());
    if (!g.ok) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, false,
                       role, id.index, 0i32);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), g.text, g.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, true,
                   role, id.index, 0i32);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE CALLEE'S `ensures` AS KNOWLEDGE (L-4): under the arguments and the
// unwrapped value, quiet; the clauses the encoder cannot express are
// dropped (assuming less is sound), the rest one hypothesis.
func:push_callee_ensures = NIL(Encoder->:e, CallEnc:ce, Term:val) never fails {
    if (ce.cd == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (!val.ok) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: ce.cd });
    if ((raw contract_count(e, cdn, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES())) == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:h = raw enc_under(e, ce.names, ce.types, ce.terms, cdn, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES(), true,
                           raw term_copy(val));
    if (h.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, h.text, h.syms); }
    pass NIL;
};

// A `pure never fails` CALLEE'S VALUE (L-3): the application of its
// uninterpreted function to the argument terms -- `|uf.<name>.<decl>|`, one
// symbol per declaration -- when every argument and the result are in the
// fragment and the callee is not a coroutine; its result's range axiom is a
// hypothesis (the value IS of that type). `term_none` otherwise.
func:uf_value = Term(Encoder->:e, CallEnc:ce, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ce.cd == 0i32) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (ce.coroutine) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: ce.cd });
    if (!(raw fn_is_pure_never_fails(e, cdn))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (!((raw is_int(e, ty)) || (raw is_bool(e, ty)))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    string:sorts = "(";
    string:app = "";
    List<int32>:syms = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...ce.terms.count) {
        if (!ce.terms.items[i].ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        int32:pt = ce.types.items[i];
        if (!((raw is_int(e, pt)) || (raw is_bool(e, pt)))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (ce.terms.items[i].is_bool != (raw is_bool(e, pt))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (i > 0i64) { sorts = string_concat(sorts, " "); app = string_concat(app, " "); }
        if (raw is_bool(e, pt)) { sorts = string_concat(sorts, "Bool"); }
        else { sorts = string_concat(sorts, "Int"); }
        app = string_concat(app, ce.terms.items[i].text);
        syms = raw syms_union(syms, ce.terms.items[i].syms);
    }
    sorts = string_concat(sorts, ")");
    string:fname = string_concat("uf.", raw intern_get(e.interns, raw decl_name(cdn)));
    string:fsym = raw smt_sym(fname, ce.cd => int64);
    int32:fi = raw sym_new_fun(e, fsym, sorts, raw is_bool(e, ty));
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, fi);
    syms = raw syms_union(syms, one);
    string:text = raw smt_app1(fsym, app);
    if (ce.terms.count == 0i64) { text = string_concat(fsym, ""); }
    if (raw is_int(e, ty)) {
        drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_range_axiom(text, raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty),
                                              raw type_is_signed(e.types, ty)), syms);
    }
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: raw is_bool(e, ty), text: move(text), syms: move(syms) };
};

// --- contracts (1.5.3 step 2; D-221, D-241, D-243, D-245, D-267, D-268) -------

// The clauses of one kind on a declaration: their count, and their
// conjunction over the current bindings -- every clause a term, or
// `term_none` when one is not (a GOAL needs every clause; a HYPOTHESIS may
// drop the ones it cannot express, `partial`, and asserts the rest).
func:contract_count = int32(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d, int32:kind) never fails {
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass 0i32; }
    int32:n = 0i32;
    int32:cc = raw fn_contract_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...cc) {
        VerifyNode:cv = raw ast_verify(e.ast, raw fn_contract(e.ast, d, i));
        if (cv.kind != VerifyKind.VerifyContractNode) { continue; }
        if ((raw contract_kind(cv)) == kind) { n = n + 1i32; }
    }
    pass n;
};

func:fn_is_pure_never_fails = bool(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d) never fails {
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass false; }
    bool:is_pure = false;
    bool:nf = false;
    int32:cc = raw fn_contract_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...cc) {
        VerifyNode:cv = raw ast_verify(e.ast, raw fn_contract(e.ast, d, i));
        if (cv.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyPure) { is_pure = true; }
        if (cv.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyNeverFails) { nf = true; }
    }
    pass (is_pure && nf);
};

func:contract_conj = Term(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d, int32:kind, bool:partial) never fails {
    Term:acc = raw term_none();
    bool:first = true;
    bool:saw_any = false;
    int32:cc = raw fn_contract_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...cc) {
        VerifyNode:cv = raw ast_verify(e.ast, raw fn_contract(e.ast, d, i));
        if (cv.kind != VerifyKind.VerifyContractNode) { continue; }
        if ((raw contract_kind(cv)) != kind) { continue; }
        saw_any = true;
        Term:c = raw enc_expr(e, raw contract_cond(cv));
        if (!(c.ok && c.is_bool)) {
            if (partial) { continue; }
            pass (raw term_none());
        }
        if (first) { acc = move(c); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, c, true); }
    }
    if (!saw_any) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
    if (first) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass acc;
};

// A loop invariant's clauses, likewise.
func:invariant_conj = Term(Encoder->:e, VerifyId:inv, bool:partial) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(inv)) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
    VerifyNode:v = raw ast_verify(e.ast, inv);
    Term:acc = raw term_none();
    bool:first = true;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw invariant_count(v))) {
        Term:c = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, v.b, i) });
        if (!(c.ok && c.is_bool)) {
            if (partial) { continue; }
            pass (raw term_none());
        }
        if (first) { acc = move(c); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, c, true); }
    }
    if ((raw invariant_count(v)) == 0i32) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
    if (first) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass acc;
};

func:invariant_clauses = int32(Encoder->:e, VerifyId:inv) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(inv)) { pass 0i32; }
    pass (raw invariant_count(raw ast_verify(e.ast, inv)));
};

// SUBSTITUTION (L-2, L-4): the declaration's contract clauses of `kind`
// encoded with its parameters bound, by position, to the given terms -- a
// fresh version of each name equal to its term (an inexpressible term an
// opaque version), so a compound argument is named once -- and `result`
// bound to `result_term`. QUIET: the clauses' own guards are the callee's
// (L-5), never this function's sites. The bindings are released after.
func:enc_under = Term(Encoder->:e, List<int32>:names, List<int32>:types, List<Term>:terms,
                      DeclNode:d, int32:kind, bool:partial, Term:result_term) never fails {
    int64:mark = raw scope_mark(e);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...names.count) {
        drop bind_define(e, names.items[i], types.items[i], raw term_copy(terms.items[i]), 0i32, true);
    }
    Term:saved_res = raw term_copy(e.result);
    e.result = raw term_copy(result_term);
    e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
    Term:t = raw contract_conj(e, d, kind, partial);
    e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
    e.result = move(saved_res);
    drop scope_release(e, mark);
    pass t;
};

// THE FUNCTION'S OWN ENTRY (L-7; D-252 as amended by D-268): its `requires`
// row -- kind `requires`, SITE_DECL the declaration, the conjunction over the
// parameters' first versions, hypotheses the range axioms -- discharged, the
// entry check is elided in place (the `.req` predicate stays uncalled). The
// clauses are encoded LOUD: a guard inside one is this function's site
// (L-5), lowered once in the predicate. Then the conjunction as a hypothesis
// (the body may assume its precondition), after the row so the goal is never
// in its own cone. One trap per clause in the predicate: the row's `traps`.
pub func:enc_entry_contracts = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    if (e.fn_decl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: e.fn_decl });
    // THE CONFORMANCE ROWS FIRST: the impl's own `requires` is their goal,
    // and the hypothesis pushed below would prove it of itself.
    drop enc_conformance(e, d);
    int32:rn = raw contract_count(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES());
    if (rn > 0i32) {
        Term:g = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), false);
        if (!g.ok) {
            List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), "", none, raw SITE_DECL(), e.fn_decl, d.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.fn_decl, rn);
            e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
            Term:h = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), true);
            e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
            if (h.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, h.text, h.syms); }
        } else {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), g.text, g.syms, raw SITE_DECL(), e.fn_decl, d.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.fn_decl, rn);
            drop hyp_push(e, g.text, g.syms);
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// CONFORMANCE (L-6): an impl method against its trait's method of the same
// name, in regions of their own so nothing leaks into the body. `requires`:
// the trait's clauses as a hypothesis over this method's parameters, the
// impl's own as the goal -- an impl may WEAKEN a precondition (trait implies
// impl). `ensures`: the impl's clauses as a hypothesis over an opaque result,
// the trait's as the goal -- an impl may STRENGTHEN a postcondition (impl
// implies trait). Both rows `conform`: no guard, an open row is reported
// (the impl's own entry and seam checks are the runtime), never a refusal.
func:enc_conformance = NIL(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d) never fails {
    if (e.impl_decl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (e.trait_ty == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:tdecl = raw type_decl_of(e.types, e.trait_ty);
    if (tdecl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:td = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: tdecl });
    int32:tmi = 0i32;
    int32:mn = raw item_member_count(e.ast, td);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...mn) {
        DeclId:mid = raw item_member(e.ast, td, i);
        DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(e.ast, mid);
        if (m.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { continue; }
        if ((raw decl_name(m)) == (raw decl_name(d))) { tmi = mid.index; }
    }
    if (tmi == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (tmi == e.fn_decl) { pass NIL; }   // an inherited default IS the trait's method
    DeclNode:tm = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: tmi });
    int32:pc = raw fn_param_count(e.ast, d);
    if (pc != (raw fn_param_count(e.ast, tm))) { pass NIL; }
    if ((pc => int64) > e.binds.count) { pass NIL; }
    List<int32>:names = raw list_init::<int32>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<int32>:types = raw list_init::<int32>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<Term>:terms = raw list_init::<Term>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int32:p in 0i32...pc) {
        DeclNode:tp = raw ast_decl(e.ast, raw fn_param(e.ast, tm, p));
        drop list_push(@names, raw decl_name(tp));
        drop list_push(@types, e.binds.items[p => int64].type_id);
        drop list_push(@terms, raw bind_term(e, p => int64));
    }
    int32:tr_n = raw contract_count(e, tm, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES());
    int32:im_n = raw contract_count(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES());
    if ((tr_n > 0i32) || (im_n > 0i32)) {
        drop region_enter(e);
        Term:th = raw enc_under(e, names, types, terms, tm, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), true, raw term_none());
        if (th.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, th.text, th.syms); }
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:ig = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), false);
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        if (ig.ok) {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), ig.text, ig.syms, raw SITE_CONF(), e.fn_decl, d.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_CONFORM(), e.fn_decl, 0i32);
        } else {
            List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), "", none, raw SITE_CONF(), e.fn_decl, d.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_CONFORM(), e.fn_decl, 0i32);
        }
        drop region_leave(e);
    }
    int32:te_n = raw contract_count(e, tm, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES());
    int32:ie_n = raw contract_count(e, d, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES());
    if ((te_n > 0i32) || (ie_n > 0i32)) {
        drop region_enter(e);
        // The trait's precondition is knowledge here too: the trait's
        // postcondition is claimed only for calls that satisfied it.
        Term:th2 = raw enc_under(e, names, types, terms, tm, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), true, raw term_none());
        if (th2.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, th2.text, th2.syms); }
        Term:r = raw term_opaque(e, e.ret_type);
        Term:saved_res = raw term_copy(e.result);
        e.result = raw term_copy(r);
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:ih = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES(), true);
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        e.result = move(saved_res);
        if (ih.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, ih.text, ih.syms); }
        Term:tg = raw enc_under(e, names, types, terms, tm, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES(), false, raw term_copy(r));
        if (tg.ok) {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_ENSURES(), tg.text, tg.syms, raw SITE_CONF(), e.fn_decl, d.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_CONFORM(), e.fn_decl, 0i32);
        } else {
            List<int32>:none2 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_ENSURES(), "", none2, raw SITE_CONF(), e.fn_decl, d.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_CONFORM(), e.fn_decl, 0i32);
        }
        drop region_leave(e);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE SEAM (L-7, L-12): at a `pass v` or a successful `return Result{...}`,
// kind `ensures`, SITE_STMT the statement, the clauses conjoined with
// `result` the value's term (opaque when the value has none; `term_none` for
// a bare `pass`, where `result` is NIL) -- encoded LOUD under the seam's
// clause context, so a guard inside a clause is this seam's own site. One
// trap per return point: `traps` 1.
func:record_seam = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, Span:at, Term:v, int32:vty, bool:has_value) never fails {
    if (e.fn_decl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: e.fn_decl });
    if ((raw contract_count(e, d, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES())) == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:saved_res = raw term_copy(e.result);
    e.result = raw term_none();
    if (has_value) {
        if (v.ok) { e.result = raw term_copy(v); }
        else { e.result = raw term_opaque(e, vty); }
    }
    e.clause_ctx = sid.index;
    Term:g = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES(), false);
    e.clause_ctx = 0i32;
    e.result = move(saved_res);
    if (!g.ok) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record_at(e, raw OK_ENSURES(), "", none, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, at, false,
                       raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop record_at(e, raw OK_ENSURES(), g.text, g.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, at, true,
                   raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
    pass NIL;
};

// The loop frame a `continue` or `break` re-enters or leaves: the innermost
// for an unlabelled one, the one carrying the label otherwise; -1 for none.
func:loop_frame = int64(Encoder->:e, int32:label) never fails {
    if (e.loop_sids.count == 0i64) { pass (0i64 - 1i64); }
    if (label == 0i32) { pass (e.loop_sids.count - 1i64); }
    int64:i = e.loop_sids.count;
    while (i > 0i64) {
        i = i - 1i64;
        if (e.loop_labels.items[i] == label) { pass i; }
    }
    pass (0i64 - 1i64);
};

// Does a `break` leave the loop whose body this is? An unlabelled one
// directly in the body, a labelled one naming the loop anywhere in it.
func:loop_has_break = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, int32:label, bool:nested, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass false; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    // A `break` INSIDE A PICK EXPRESSION'S ARM (DEF-26, 1.5.4 step 0): the
    // arms are statements inside an expression, found through the one
    // enumeration of a statement's expressions.
    List<int32>:xs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop stmt_expr_ids(e.ast, s, @xs);
    for (int64:xi in 0i64...xs.count) {
        if (raw expr_has_break(e, ExprId{ index: xs.items[xi] }, label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBreakStmt) {
        if ((raw stmt_label(s)) == 0i32) { pass (!nested); }
        pass ((raw stmt_label(s)) == label);
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
            if (raw loop_has_break(e, ch, label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_then(s), label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_else(s), label, nested, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt)   { pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s), label, true, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw arm_body(arm), label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

// The `break` finder's descent into an EXPRESSION: a pick expression's arms
// are statements (DEF-26); every other kind is searched for nested ones.
func:expr_has_break = bool(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, int32:label, bool:nested, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...n.c) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, n.b, a));
            if (raw expr_has_break(e, raw arm_guard(arm), label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
            if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw arm_body(arm), label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
    }
    List<int32>:kids = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop expr_children(e, n, @kids);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...kids.count) {
        if (raw expr_has_break(e, ExprId{ index: kids.items[i] }, label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// A LOOP'S COUNTER as `walk_loop` receives it (L-11, L-12): kind 0 none, 1 a
// `for` binding by name (`ranged` when the iterable is a range: `start` and
// `limit` its captured bounds, the limit exclusive, the step 1, ascending),
// 2 a counted loop's `$` (`start`, `limit`, `step` captured, `asc` the
// direction term, `lit_step` the numeral step's value or 0).
struct:Counter = {
    int32:kind;
    int32:name;
    bool:ranged;
    Term:start;
    Term:limit;
    Term:step;
    Term:asc;
    int64:lit_step;
};

func:counter_none = Counter() never fails {
    pass Counter{ kind: 0i32, name: 0i32, ranged: false, start: raw term_none(), limit: raw term_none(),
                  step: raw term_none(), asc: raw term_none(), lit_step: 0i64 };
};

// CAPTURE a term at entry (L-11; D-234's rule): a fresh anonymous symbol of
// the type, defined equal to the term when the term exists -- what the
// body assigns later cannot move it, exactly as the emitter's slots hold the
// bound and the step across iterations.
func:term_capture = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty, Term:t) never fails {
    Term:s = raw term_opaque(e, ty);
    if (!s.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (t.ok && (t.is_bool == s.is_bool)) {
        drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", s.text, t.text), raw syms_union(s.syms, t.syms));
    }
    pass s;
};

// A fresh `$` symbol (`|$.k|`, the anonymous counter as k), int64 -- the
// checker's type for a counter.
func:dollar_fresh = Term(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    int32:i64t = raw tt_int(e.types, 64i32, true);
    e.anon = e.anon + 1i32;
    string:nm = raw smt_sym("$", e.anon => int64);
    int32:idx = raw sym_new(e, nm, i64t);
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, idx);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: move(nm), syms: move(one) };
};

func:term_not = Term(Term:t) never fails {
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", t.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(t.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
};

// THE COUNTER'S RANGE IN THE BODY (L-11): `start <= $ < limit` ascending,
// `limit < $ <= start` descending, each under the direction; on a numeral
// step the residue class (`mod` by a numeral is linear).
func:push_dollar_range = NIL(Encoder->:e, Counter:c, Term:d) never fails {
    if (!(d.ok && c.start.ok && c.limit.ok && c.asc.ok)) { pass NIL; }
    Term:up = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2("<=", c.start, d, true), raw term_app2("<", d, c.limit, true), true);
    Term:down = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2("<", c.limit, d, true), raw term_app2("<=", d, c.start, true), true);
    Term:nasc = raw term_not(c.asc);
    Term:h1 = raw term_app2("=>", c.asc, up, true);
    Term:h2 = raw term_app2("=>", nasc, down, true);
    drop hyp_push(e, h1.text, h1.syms);
    drop hyp_push(e, h2.text, h2.syms);
    if (c.lit_step > 0i64) {
        Term:s = raw term_lit(int_to_string(c.lit_step), false);
        Term:ru = raw term_app2("=", raw term_app2("mod", raw term_app2("-", d, c.start, false), s, false), raw term_lit("0", false), true);
        Term:rd = raw term_app2("=", raw term_app2("mod", raw term_app2("-", c.start, d, false), s, false), raw term_lit("0", false), true);
        Term:h3 = raw term_app2("=>", c.asc, ru, true);
        Term:h4 = raw term_app2("=>", nasc, rd, true);
        drop hyp_push(e, h3.text, h3.syms);
        drop hyp_push(e, h4.text, h4.syms);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE COUNTER AFTER THE LOOP (L-11): past the limit -- by less than a numeral
// step -- and past the start, under the direction; the residue class again.
// A zero-iteration loop (`start == limit`) exits with the start, which
// satisfies every one of these.
func:push_dollar_exit = NIL(Encoder->:e, Counter:c, Term:x) never fails {
    if (!(x.ok && c.start.ok && c.limit.ok && c.asc.ok)) { pass NIL; }
    Term:nasc = raw term_not(c.asc);
    Term:up = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2(">=", x, c.limit, true), raw term_app2(">=", x, c.start, true), true);
    Term:down = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2("<=", x, c.limit, true), raw term_app2("<=", x, c.start, true), true);
    Term:h1 = raw term_app2("=>", c.asc, up, true);
    Term:h2 = raw term_app2("=>", nasc, down, true);
    drop hyp_push(e, h1.text, h1.syms);
    drop hyp_push(e, h2.text, h2.syms);
    if (c.lit_step > 0i64) {
        Term:s = raw term_lit(int_to_string(c.lit_step), false);
        Term:lu = raw term_app2("<", x, raw term_app2("+", c.limit, s, false), true);
        Term:ld = raw term_app2(">", x, raw term_app2("-", c.limit, s, false), true);
        Term:ru = raw term_app2("=", raw term_app2("mod", raw term_app2("-", x, c.start, false), s, false), raw term_lit("0", false), true);
        Term:rd = raw term_app2("=", raw term_app2("mod", raw term_app2("-", c.start, x, false), s, false), raw term_lit("0", false), true);
        Term:h3 = raw term_app2("=>", c.asc, raw term_app2("and", lu, ru, true), true);
        Term:h4 = raw term_app2("=>", nasc, raw term_app2("and", ld, rd, true), true);
        drop hyp_push(e, h3.text, h3.syms);
        drop hyp_push(e, h4.text, h4.syms);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE INCREMENTED COUNTER the head will see (L-11): `$ + step` ascending,
// `$ - step` descending; a range binding's is `i + 1`.
func:counter_next = Term(Encoder->:e, Term:cur, Term:step, Term:asc) never fails {
    if (!(cur.ok && step.ok)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    Term:up = raw term_app2("+", cur, step, false);
    if (!asc.ok) { pass up; }
    Term:down = raw term_app2("-", cur, step, false);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app3("ite", asc.text, up.text, down.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(asc.syms, raw syms_union(up.syms, down.syms)) };
};

// SUBSTITUTE the incremented counter for a head-visit row (the preservation
// row, a `continue`'s): `$`'s entry in `dollars` set to the next value, a
// range binding given a new version equal to `i + 1` (L-11, L-12).
func:counter_advance = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:kind, int32:name, Term:step, Term:asc, int64:dollar) never fails {
    if (kind == 2i32) {
        if ((dollar >= 0i64) && (dollar < e.dollars.count)) {
            Term:cur = raw term_copy(e.dollars.items[dollar]);
            e.dollars.items[dollar] = raw counter_next(e, cur, step, asc);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (kind == 1i32) {
        int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, name);
        if (bi < 0i64) { pass NIL; }
        Term:cur = raw bind_term(e, bi);
        if (!cur.ok) { pass NIL; }
        drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("+", cur, raw term_lit("1", false), false));
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A LOOP (L-8, L-9): the ENTRY row -- kind `invariant`, SITE_STMT the loop
// statement, the conjunction over the versions before any havoc, LOUD under
// the loop's clause context (a guard inside a clause is the head's site,
// lowered once) -- then the body's assigned names havoced, and inside the
// body's region the invariant as a hypothesis over the havoced versions and,
// for `while`/`when`, the condition too (both dominate only the body); at
// the body's end the PRESERVATION row keyed at the body block, and one at
// every `continue` that re-enters this loop (`walk_stmt`); after the loop
// the names havoced again and, when nothing `break`s out, the invariant as a
// hypothesis once more -- it holds at every head visit and the exit is one.
// The condition's negation is NOT pushed (1.5.4's path condition). All of a
// loop's rows share its group and its clause count: the head's check elides
// only when every one is discharged, and keeps one trap per clause.
func:walk_loop = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, VerifyId:inv, StmtId:body, ExprId:cond,
                     int32:label, Counter:ctr) never fails {
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    List<int32>:assigned = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop collect_assigned(e, body, @assigned);
    // THE COUNTER (L-11, L-12): a `for` binding is an assigned name of its
    // loop (havoced with the rest); `$` starts at its start for the entry row.
    if (ctr.kind == 1i32) { drop list_push(@assigned, ctr.name); }
    int64:dollar = 0i64 - 1i64;
    if (ctr.kind == 2i32) {
        dollar = e.dollars.count;
        drop list_push(@e.dollars, raw term_copy(ctr.start));
    }
    int32:nc = raw invariant_clauses(e, inv);
    if (nc > 0i32) {
        e.clause_ctx = sid.index;
        Term:g0 = raw invariant_conj(e, inv, false);
        e.clause_ctx = 0i32;
        if (g0.ok) {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), g0.text, g0.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, nc);
        } else {
            List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), "", none, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, nc);
        }
    }
    drop invalidate(e, assigned);
    drop region_enter(e);
    // THE COUNTER IN THE BODY (L-11, L-12): a fresh `$` inside its range; a
    // range binding's havoced version inside its bounds.
    if (ctr.kind == 2i32) {
        Term:d = raw dollar_fresh(e);
        e.dollars.items[dollar] = raw term_copy(d);
        drop push_dollar_range(e, ctr, d);
    }
    if ((ctr.kind == 1i32) && ctr.ranged) {
        int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, ctr.name);
        if (bi >= 0i64) {
            Term:iv = raw bind_term(e, bi);
            if (iv.ok && ctr.start.ok && ctr.limit.ok) {
                Term:rf = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2("<=", ctr.start, iv, true), raw term_app2("<", iv, ctr.limit, true), true);
                drop hyp_push(e, rf.text, rf.syms);
            }
        }
    }
    if (nc > 0i32) {
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:h = raw invariant_conj(e, inv, true);
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        if (h.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, h.text, h.syms); }
    }
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(cond))) {
        Term:wc = raw enc_expr(e, cond);
        if (wc.ok && wc.is_bool) { drop hyp_push(e, wc.text, wc.syms); }
    }
    drop list_push(@e.loop_sids, sid.index);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_labels, label);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_invs, inv.index);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_ckind, ctr.kind);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_cname, ctr.name);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_cstep, raw term_copy(ctr.step));
    drop list_push(@e.loop_casc, raw term_copy(ctr.asc));
    drop list_push(@e.loop_cdollar, dollar);
    drop walk_block(e, body);
    e.loop_sids.count = e.loop_sids.count - 1i64;
    e.loop_labels.count = e.loop_labels.count - 1i64;
    e.loop_invs.count = e.loop_invs.count - 1i64;
    e.loop_ckind.count = e.loop_ckind.count - 1i64;
    e.loop_cname.count = e.loop_cname.count - 1i64;
    e.loop_cstep.count = e.loop_cstep.count - 1i64;
    e.loop_casc.count = e.loop_casc.count - 1i64;
    e.loop_cdollar.count = e.loop_cdollar.count - 1i64;
    if (nc > 0i32) {
        StmtNode:bs = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, body);
        // THE PRESERVATION ROW SEES THE INCREMENTED COUNTER (L-11, L-12).
        if ((ctr.kind == 2i32) || ((ctr.kind == 1i32) && ctr.ranged)) {
            drop counter_advance(e, ctr.kind, ctr.name, ctr.step, ctr.asc, dollar);
        }
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:gp = raw invariant_conj(e, inv, false);
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        if (gp.ok) {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), gp.text, gp.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), body.index, bs.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, nc);
        } else {
            List<int32>:none2 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), "", none2, raw SITE_STMT(), body.index, bs.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, nc);
        }
    }
    drop region_leave(e);
    drop invalidate(e, assigned);
    bool:no_break = !(raw loop_has_break(e, body, label, false, 64i32));
    // THE COUNTER AFTER THE LOOP (L-11, L-12): `$`'s exit value; a range
    // binding's fresh version exactly at its bound (`ite (< lo hi) hi lo`).
    if (ctr.kind == 2i32) {
        Term:x = raw dollar_fresh(e);
        e.dollars.items[dollar] = raw term_copy(x);
        drop push_dollar_exit(e, ctr, x);
    }
    if ((ctr.kind == 1i32) && ctr.ranged) {
        int64:bi2 = raw bind_find(e, ctr.name);
        if (bi2 >= 0i64) {
            Term:iv2 = raw bind_term(e, bi2);
            if (iv2.ok && ctr.start.ok && ctr.limit.ok) {
                Term:xv = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false,
                                text: raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2("<", ctr.start.text, ctr.limit.text), ctr.limit.text, ctr.start.text),
                                syms: raw syms_union(ctr.start.syms, ctr.limit.syms) };
                Term:xe = raw term_app2("=", iv2, xv, true);
                drop hyp_push(e, xe.text, xe.syms);
            }
        }
    }
    if (nc > 0i32) {
        if (no_break) {
            e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
            Term:h2 = raw invariant_conj(e, inv, true);
            e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
            if (h2.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, h2.text, h2.syms); }
        }
    }
    // THE CONDITION IS FALSE AFTER A LOOP NOTHING `break`s OUT OF (L-4): the
    // exit is a head visit that found it false, over the post-havoc versions.
    // Encoded QUIET: its sites were recorded once, inside the body region.
    if (no_break && (!(raw expr_is_none(cond)))) {
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:wc2 = raw enc_expr(e, cond);
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        if (wc2.ok && wc2.is_bool) { drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app1("not", wc2.text), wc2.syms); }
    }
    if (ctr.kind == 2i32) { e.dollars.count = e.dollars.count - 1i64; }
    pass NIL;
};

// An assignment to a NAME: the new version, defined by the operator's term
// where the operands are encodable (the compound spellings through the
// truncating definitions, P-17; a `/=` or `%=` records its division first).
// The caller records the write point AFTER this (L-7's order).
func:assign_ident = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtNode:s, TokenKind:op, ExprId:target,
                        int32:name, Term:rhs) never fails {
    if (op == TokenKind.OpAssign) { drop bind_assign(e, name, rhs); pass NIL; }
    // Compound: the current value op the right-hand side.
    Term:prior = raw enc_expr(e, target);
    int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, name);
    int32:lt = 0i32;
    if (bi >= 0i64) { lt = e.binds.items[bi].type_id; }
    if (!(raw is_int(e, lt))) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_none()); pass NIL; }
    if ((op == TokenKind.OpSlashAssign) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercentAssign)) {
        drop record_division(e, lt, prior, rhs, target.index, s.span);
        if (!(prior.ok && rhs.ok)) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_none()); pass NIL; }
        if (!(raw term_is_numeral(rhs))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
        if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, lt)) {
            e.uses_sdiv = true;
            e.nonlinear = true;
            if (op == TokenKind.OpSlashAssign) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("npk_sdiv", prior, rhs, false)); }
            else { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("npk_srem", prior, rhs, false)); }
            pass NIL;
        }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpSlashAssign) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("div", prior, rhs, false)); }
        else { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("mod", prior, rhs, false)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (!(prior.ok && rhs.ok)) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_none()); pass NIL; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPlusAssign)  { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("+", prior, rhs, false)); pass NIL; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpMinusAssign) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("-", prior, rhs, false)); pass NIL; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpStarAssign) {
        if (!((raw term_is_numeral(prior)) || (raw term_is_numeral(rhs)))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
        drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("*", prior, rhs, false));
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_none());
    pass NIL;
};

func:term_copy = Term(Term:t) never fails {
    List<int32>:s = raw list_init::<int32>(t.syms.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...t.syms.count) { drop list_push(@s, t.syms.items[i]); }
    pass Term{ ok: t.ok, is_bool: t.is_bool, text: string_concat(t.text, ""), syms: move(s) };
};

// A simd division: the any-lane guard's site, `unencoded` (P-12).
func:record_unencoded_division = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:elem, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop record(e, raw OK_DIV_ZERO(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
    if (raw is_int(e, elem)) {
        if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, elem)) {
            drop record(e, raw OK_DIV_MIN(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the expression walk -------------------------------------------------------------------

// The child expressions of a node, by kind -- ONE place knows the layouts
// (AST_REFERENCE §3; the parser's construction sites). A kind not listed here
// has no expression children the walk can see, which for a kind that DOES
// have some would be a missed site: the harness's every-guard-has-a-row
// cross-check is what catches that class.
func:expr_children = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprNode:n, List<int32>->:out) never fails {
    ExprKind:k = n.kind;
    if ((k == ExprKind.ExprBinaryExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprSafeUnwrapExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprNullCoalesceExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprEmphaticUnwrapExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprDefaultsExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprPipeExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprResultLiteralExpr)) {
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        if (n.b != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.b); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprTernaryExpr) {
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        if (n.b != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.b); }
        if (n.c != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.c); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((k == ExprKind.ExprUnaryExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprPostfixExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprSpreadExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprMoveExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprIsErrExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprComptimeExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprDropExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprRelayExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprDynCastExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprAwaitExpr)) {
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        int32:g = raw expr_generic_count(n);
        for (int32:i in g...n.c) { drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, i)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) {
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        for (int32:i2 in 0i32...n.c) { drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, i2)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        int32:g2 = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
        for (int32:i3 in g2...n.c) { drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, i3)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((k == ExprKind.ExprArrayLiteralExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprTemplateLiteral)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprVectorCtorExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr)) {
        if (k == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
            // a value-pick's arms are statements; its selector is the one expression
            if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
            pass NIL;
        }
        for (int32:i4 in 0i32...n.c) { drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, i4)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        int32:pairs = n.c / 2i32;
        for (int32:i5 in 0i32...pairs) {
            drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, (i5 * 2i32) + 1i32));
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Walk the children for sites only; the value is opaque.
func:walk_children = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    List<int32>:kids = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop expr_children(e, n, @kids);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...kids.count) {
        Term:t = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: kids.items[i] });
    }
    pass NIL;
};

pub func:enc_expr = Term(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    int32:ty = raw ty_of(e, id);

    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) {
        if (!(raw is_int(e, ty))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, ty)) { pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(n.payload), false)); }
        pass (raw term_lit(raw u64_decimal(n.payload =>! uint64), false));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBoolLiteral) {
        if (n.payload != 0i64) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
        pass (raw term_lit("false", true));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, n.payload =>! int32);
        if (bi >= 0i64) {
            // UNDER `old(...)` (D-243): the binding's entry version.
            int32:want = e.binds.items[bi].sym;
            if (e.at_entry) { want = e.binds.items[bi].entry; }
            if (want >= 0i32) {
                int32:si = want;
                List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                drop list_push(@one, si);
                pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: e.syms.items[si => int64].is_bool,
                           text: raw sym_text(e, si), syms: move(one) };
            }
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBinaryExpr) {
        TokenKind:op = raw expr_op(n);
        Term:a = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_lhs(n));
        // THE RIGHT-HAND SIDE OF `&&`/`||` IS AN ARM (1.5.4 step 2, L-10): it
        // runs only when the left decided nothing, so its sites and its
        // symbols live under `a` (or `(not a)`), in a region of their own
        // whose facts come back guarded.
        Term:b = raw term_none();
        if (((op == TokenKind.OpAndAnd) || (op == TokenKind.OpOrOr)) && a.ok && a.is_bool) {
            Term:ac = raw term_copy(a);
            if (op == TokenKind.OpOrOr) {
                ac = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", a.text),
                           syms: raw syms_union(a.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
            }
            drop region_enter_cond(e, ac);
            drop hyp_push(e, ac.text, ac.syms);
            b = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(n));
            drop region_leave(e);
        } else {
            b = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(n));
        }
        int32:lt = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_lhs(n));
        if ((op == TokenKind.OpAndAnd) || (op == TokenKind.OpOrOr)) {
            if (a.ok && b.ok && a.is_bool && b.is_bool) {
                if (op == TokenKind.OpAndAnd) { pass (raw term_app2("and", a, b, true)); }
                pass (raw term_app2("or", a, b, true));
            }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        if (raw is_int(e, lt)) {
            bool:divlike = ((op == TokenKind.OpSlash) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercent));
            if (divlike) {
                drop record_division(e, lt, a, b, id.index, n.span);
                if (!(a.ok && b.ok)) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
                if (!(raw term_is_numeral(b))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
                if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, lt)) {
                    e.uses_sdiv = true;
                    e.nonlinear = true;
                    if (op == TokenKind.OpSlash) { pass (raw term_app2("npk_sdiv", a, b, false)); }
                    pass (raw term_app2("npk_srem", a, b, false));
                }
                if (op == TokenKind.OpSlash) { pass (raw term_app2("div", a, b, false)); }
                pass (raw term_app2("mod", a, b, false));
            }
            if (!(a.ok && b.ok)) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
            if (a.is_bool || b.is_bool) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpPlus)  { pass (raw term_app2("+", a, b, false)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpMinus) { pass (raw term_app2("-", a, b, false)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpStar) {
                if (!((raw term_is_numeral(a)) || (raw term_is_numeral(b)))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
                pass (raw term_app2("*", a, b, false));
            }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpLt)    { pass (raw term_app2("<", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpLtEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("<=", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpGt)    { pass (raw term_app2(">", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpGtEq)  { pass (raw term_app2(">=", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpEqEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("=", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq) { pass (raw term_app2("distinct", a, b, true)); }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        if (raw is_bool(e, lt)) {
            if (a.ok && b.ok && a.is_bool && b.is_bool) {
                if (op == TokenKind.OpEqEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("=", a, b, true)); }
                if (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq) { pass (raw term_app2("distinct", a, b, true)); }
            }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        if (lt != 0i32) {
            if ((raw type_kind(e.types, lt)) == (raw TY_SIMD())) {
                if ((op == TokenKind.OpSlash) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercent)) {
                    drop record_unencoded_division(e, raw type_elem(e.types, lt), id.index, n.span);
                }
            }
        }
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUnaryExpr) {
        TokenKind:uop = raw expr_op(n);
        Term:o = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        if (!o.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
        if ((uop == TokenKind.OpMinus) && (raw is_int(e, ty)) && (!o.is_bool)) {
            pass (raw term_app2("-", raw term_lit("0", false), o, false));
        }
        if ((uop == TokenKind.OpBang) && o.is_bool) {
            pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", o.text),
                       syms: raw syms_union(o.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprTernaryExpr) {
        // THE TWO BRANCHES ARE ARMS (L-10): each under its condition, in a
        // region of its own (the emitter runs only the taken one, D-145).
        Term:c = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        bool:tc = c.ok && c.is_bool;
        Term:nc = raw term_none();
        if (tc) {
            nc = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", c.text),
                       syms: raw syms_union(c.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        if (tc) { drop region_enter_cond(e, c); drop hyp_push(e, c.text, c.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        Term:t1 = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.b });
        drop region_leave(e);
        if (tc) { drop region_enter_cond(e, nc); drop hyp_push(e, nc.text, nc.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        Term:t2 = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.c });
        drop region_leave(e);
        if (c.ok && t1.ok && t2.ok && c.is_bool && (t1.is_bool == t2.is_bool)) {
            pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: t1.is_bool,
                       text: raw smt_app3("ite", c.text, t1.text, t2.text),
                       syms: raw syms_union(c.syms, raw syms_union(t1.syms, t2.syms)) };
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) {
        // `=>` between integers is value-preserving by the checker's own rule
        // (a lossy `=>` is refused), so the term is the operand's.
        Term:ct = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        int32:st = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        if (ct.ok && (raw is_int(e, st)) && (raw is_int(e, ty)) && (!ct.is_bool)) { pass ct; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMoveExpr) {
        Term:mt = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        if (mt.ok) { pass mt; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // `$` -- THE RULE'S SUBJECT (1.5.2 step 3, L-8): inside `enc_rule` it is
    // the term the rule is being instantiated over; outside one it is the
    // innermost counted loop's counter (1.5.4 step 3, L-11): its start at
    // the entry row, a fresh in-range symbol in the body, the incremented
    // value at the preservation and `continue` rows, the exit value after.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIterationVarExpr) {
        if (e.subject.ok) { pass (raw term_copy(e.subject)); }
        if (e.dollars.count > 0i64) {
            Term:top = raw term_copy(e.dollars.items[e.dollars.count - 1i64]);
            if (top.ok) { pass top; }
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // A CALL (1.5.2 step 3, L-10; 1.5.3 step 2, D-268): the receiver and
    // every argument are sites, encoded ONCE; a callee the checker recorded
    // gets its `limit-subsume` row and its `requires` row over the argument
    // terms; the value -- a `Result`, or a bare value nothing unwrapped -- is
    // opaque. The unwrap arms below are where a known callee's value becomes
    // an uninterpreted function and its `ensures` becomes knowledge.
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr)) {
        CallEnc:ce = raw enc_call(e, id, n);
        drop record_call_rows(e, id, n, ce);
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // `result` (D-245): the value being passed, while an `ensures` is
    // encoded at a seam; `old(e)` (D-243): the operand over the entry
    // versions. Outside those contexts each is opaque -- and the checker
    // admits them nowhere else.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprResultValueExpr) {
        if (e.result.ok) { pass (raw term_copy(e.result)); }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprOldExpr) {
        bool:saved_entry = e.at_entry;
        e.at_entry = true;
        Term:ot = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        e.at_entry = saved_entry;
        if (ot.ok) { pass ot; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // AN UNWRAP THAT CONTINUES ONLY ON SUCCESS (1.5.3 step 2, L-3, L-4):
    // `raw f(...)`, `f(...) ?! E`, `relay f(...)`, each over a plain or an
    // awaited call. The call's rows are recorded as above; the VALUE is an
    // uninterpreted function application when the callee is `pure never
    // fails` over the fragment (a `raw` call: equal inputs, equal outputs,
    // D-242), else a fresh opaque symbol; and the callee's `ensures` is
    // pushed as a hypothesis over the arguments and that value -- sound
    // because the callee's seam guards or proves it before any continuing
    // execution reaches here. `?|` pushes nothing: its value may be the
    // default.
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprEmphaticUnwrapExpr)
        || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRelayExpr)) {
        ExprId:inner = ExprId{ index: n.a };
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(inner))) {
            ExprNode:inn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, inner);
            if (inn.kind == ExprKind.ExprAwaitExpr) {
                inner = ExprId{ index: inn.a };
                if (!(raw expr_is_none(inner))) { inn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, inner); }
            }
            if ((!(raw expr_is_none(inner)))
                && ((inn.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) || (inn.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr))) {
                CallEnc:uce = raw enc_call(e, inner, inn);
                drop record_call_rows(e, inner, inn, uce);
                if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprEmphaticUnwrapExpr) {
                    Term:eb = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.b });
                }
                Term:val = raw term_none();
                if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr) { val = raw uf_value(e, uce, ty); }
                if (!val.ok) { val = raw term_opaque(e, ty); }
                drop push_callee_ensures(e, uce, val);
                pass val;
            }
        }
        drop walk_children(e, n);
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // A PICK EXPRESSION (DEF-26, 1.5.4 step 0): the selector a site, every
    // arm walked as the statement form's (their guard sites, their bodies'
    // sites and definitions, in regions of their own), the names the arms
    // assign invalidated after; the value opaque until 1.5.4 step 2.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        Term:psel = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        Term:pval = raw walk_pick_arms(e, n.b, n.c, psel, raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: n.a }), true);
        if (pval.ok && (pval.is_bool == (raw is_bool(e, ty))) && ((raw is_int(e, ty)) || (raw is_bool(e, ty)))) { pass pval; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // Everything else: the value is opaque, the children are still sites.
    drop walk_children(e, n);
    pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
};

// --- the statement walk --------------------------------------------------------------------

// Names an assignment statement inside `sid` targets (recursively), so a
// construct's exit can invalidate exactly what it may have changed.
func:collect_assigned = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, List<int32>->:out) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    // THE STATEMENT'S EXPRESSIONS FIRST (DEF-26, 1.5.4 step 0): a pick
    // EXPRESSION's arms are statements that assign, and they sit inside an
    // initialiser, a right-hand side, an operand -- `stmt_expr_ids` is the
    // one enumeration of where.
    List<int32>:xs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop stmt_expr_ids(e.ast, s, @xs);
    for (int64:xi in 0i64...xs.count) {
        drop collect_assigned_expr(e, ExprId{ index: xs.items[xi] }, out, 64i32);
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        ExprNode:t = raw ast_expr(e.ast, raw stmt_target(s));
        if (t.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { drop list_push(out, t.payload =>! int32); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            drop collect_assigned(e, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) }, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_then(s), out);
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_else(s), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s), out); pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt)   { drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s), out); pass NIL; }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s), out);
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), out);
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            drop collect_assigned(e, raw arm_body(arm), out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        drop collect_assigned(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index }, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A PICK EXPRESSION'S ARMS assign like a statement's (DEF-26): every arm's
// body collected, its guard and the selector searched for nested ones.
func:collect_assigned_expr = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, List<int32>->:out, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...n.c) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, n.b, a));
            drop collect_assigned_expr(e, raw arm_guard(arm), out, fuel - 1i32);
            drop collect_assigned(e, raw arm_body(arm), out);
        }
    }
    List<int32>:kids = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop expr_children(e, n, @kids);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...kids.count) {
        drop collect_assigned_expr(e, ExprId{ index: kids.items[i] }, out, fuel - 1i32);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// The root name of a place (`x`, `x.f`, `x[i]`, …), or 0.
func:place_root_name = int32(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = id;
    int32:fuel = 64i32;
    while (fuel > 0i32) {
        fuel = fuel - 1i32;
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass 0i32; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, cur);
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass (n.payload =>! int32); }
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr)
            || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr)) {
            cur = ExprId{ index: n.a };
            continue;
        }
        pass 0i32;
    }
    pass 0i32;
};

// Every name whose address is taken (`@x`, `$$m x`, `$$i x`, through any
// place path) anywhere under `id`.
func:collect_escaped_expr = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr)) {
        int32:root = raw place_root_name(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        if (root != 0i32) { drop list_push(@e.escaped, root); }
    }
    // A PICK EXPRESSION's arms are statements (DEF-26): walked as a statement's.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...n.c) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, n.b, a));
            drop collect_escaped_expr(e, raw arm_guard(arm));
            drop collect_escaped(e, raw arm_body(arm));
        }
    }
    List<int32>:kids = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop expr_children(e, n, @kids);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...kids.count) { drop collect_escaped_expr(e, ExprId{ index: kids.items[i] }); }
    pass NIL;
};

func:collect_escaped = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    // THE EXPRESSIONS THROUGH THE ONE ENUMERATION (DEF-26), then the bodies.
    List<int32>:xs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop stmt_expr_ids(e.ast, s, @xs);
    for (int64:xi in 0i64...xs.count) { drop collect_escaped_expr(e, ExprId{ index: xs.items[xi] }); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            drop collect_escaped(e, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) });
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_then(s));
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_else(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s)); pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) { drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s)); pass NIL; }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s));
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s));
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            drop collect_escaped(e, raw arm_body(arm));
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        drop collect_escaped(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index });
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Register a pattern's bindings as symbol-less bindings for the arm's scope.
func:bind_pattern = NIL(Encoder->:e, PatNode:p) never fails {
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatStructDestructure) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw pat_bind_count(p))) {
            Bind:b = Bind{ name: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw pat_bind_start(p), i), sym: 0i32 - 1i32, type_id: 0i32, rule: 0i32, entry: 0i32 - 1i32 };
            drop list_push(@e.binds, move(b));
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatEnumDestructure) {
        for (int32:j in 0i32...(raw pat_enum_bind_count(e.ast, p))) {
            Bind:b2 = Bind{ name: raw pat_enum_bind(e.ast, p, j), sym: 0i32 - 1i32, type_id: 0i32, rule: 0i32, entry: 0i32 - 1i32 };
            drop list_push(@e.binds, move(b2));
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE ARMS OF A `pick`, EITHER FORM (DEF-26, 1.5.4 step 0): each in a region
// of its own with its pattern's names bound symbol-less, its guard a site,
// its body walked, the bindings restored between arms. The statement form
// had this inline since 1.5.0; the expression form's arms were never walked,
// so a guard site inside one had no row (P-12 broken) -- one helper, both
// spellings (1.5.2c's lesson).
//
// THE ARMS' CONDITIONS (1.5.4 step 1, L-3): a value pattern is `(= sel v)`,
// a range `(and (<= lo sel) (< sel hi))` (`<=` when inclusive), a wildcard
// the negation of every arm before it when each has a condition; a
// destructure, an ERR pattern, a selector outside the fragment: none. Inside
// arm i's region its own condition holds and, since arms are tried in
// order, so does the negation of every earlier arm's. A `where` guard is a
// fact inside its arm once encoded there (it ran only when the pattern
// matched). When ANY arm carries a guard, only each arm's own pattern is
// pushed -- a guarded arm's failure is not something the patterns alone
// express -- and when a `fall` sits anywhere in the pick, no arm gets a
// condition at all: a target arm is entered from another arm.
func:walk_pick_arms = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:start, int32:count, Term:sel, int32:sel_ty, bool:want_value) never fails {
    bool:any_guard = false;
    bool:any_fall = false;
    for (int32:a0 in 0i32...count) {
        StmtNode:arm0 = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, start, a0));
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(raw arm_guard(arm0)))) { any_guard = true; }
        if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw arm_body(arm0), 64i32)) { any_fall = true; }
    }
    bool:sel_ok = sel.ok;
    if (any_fall) { sel_ok = false; }
    // The pattern conditions, in the PARENT region (a pattern's value is a
    // constant the selector is compared with on every path), one per arm.
    List<Term>:conds = raw list_init::<Term>((count => int64) + 1i64);
    bool:all_ok = true;
    for (int32:a1 in 0i32...count) {
        StmtNode:arm1 = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, start, a1));
        Term:ci = raw term_none();
        if (sel_ok) { ci = raw pattern_cond(e, raw ast_pat(e.ast, raw arm_pattern(arm1)), sel, sel_ty, conds, all_ok); }
        if (!ci.ok) { all_ok = false; }
        drop list_push(@conds, move(ci));
    }
    List<int32>:snap = raw snapshot(e);
    // THE MERGE'S INPUTS (L-8, L-9): each arm's end versions, whether it
    // completes (falls through -- for a pick expression, to its trailing
    // `give`), and the `give` term of a completing arm. A `give` anywhere
    // but as an arm's last statement leaves the arm through a nested
    // construct: the versions and the value are then a havoc and opaque.
    List<List<int32>>:snaps = raw list_init::<List<int32>>((count => int64) + 1i64);
    List<bool>:fts = raw list_init::<bool>((count => int64) + 1i64);
    List<Term>:give_terms = raw list_init::<Term>((count => int64) + 1i64);
    bool:nested_give = false;
    for (int32:a in 0i32...count) {
        StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, start, a));
        StmtId:body = raw arm_body(arm);
        int64:mark = raw scope_mark(e);
        Term:region_c = raw term_none();
        if (conds.items[a => int64].ok && (!any_guard)) { region_c = raw term_copy(conds.items[a => int64]); }
        if (region_c.ok) { drop region_enter_cond(e, region_c); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        drop bind_pattern(e, raw ast_pat(e.ast, raw arm_pattern(arm)));
        if (conds.items[a => int64].ok) {
            drop hyp_push(e, conds.items[a => int64].text, conds.items[a => int64].syms);
        }
        if (!any_guard) {
            for (int32:j in 0i32...a) {
                if (conds.items[j => int64].ok) {
                    drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app1("not", conds.items[j => int64].text), conds.items[j => int64].syms);
                }
            }
        }
        Term:g = raw enc_expr(e, raw arm_guard(arm));
        if (g.ok && g.is_bool && (!any_fall)) { drop hyp_push(e, g.text, g.syms); }
        e.last_give = raw term_none();
        drop walk_block(e, body);
        drop region_leave(e);
        drop scope_release(e, mark);
        drop list_push(@snaps, raw snapshot(e));
        bool:trailing = raw block_ends_in_give(e, body);
        if (raw stmt_has_nested_give(e, body, 64i32)) { nested_give = true; }
        if (trailing) {
            drop list_push(@fts, raw block_reaches_last(e, body));
            drop list_push(@give_terms, raw term_copy(e.last_give));
        } else {
            drop list_push(@fts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, body, 64i32));
            drop list_push(@give_terms, raw term_none());
        }
        drop restore(e, snap);
    }
    e.last_give = raw term_none();
    // THE MERGE (L-8): every arm's condition a term (a wildcard's is the
    // negation of the ones before it), no guard, no `fall`, no nested
    // `give`; else the havoc the walk did before this step.
    bool:mergeable = all_ok && (!any_guard) && (!any_fall) && (!nested_give);
    if (nested_give) {
        List<int32>:pa = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
        for (int32:a2 in 0i32...count) {
            StmtNode:arm2 = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, start, a2));
            drop collect_assigned(e, raw arm_body(arm2), @pa);
        }
        drop invalidate(e, pa);
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    drop merge_arms(e, conds, snaps, fts, snap, mergeable);
    // THE VALUE (L-9): the chain over the completing arms' `give` terms.
    if (!(want_value && mergeable)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    Term:val = raw term_none();
    bool:have = false;
    int32:k = count;
    while (k > 0i32) {
        k = k - 1i32;
        if (!fts.items[k => int64]) { continue; }
        Term:gk = raw term_copy(give_terms.items[k => int64]);
        if (!gk.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (!have) { val = move(gk); have = true; continue; }
        if (gk.is_bool != val.is_bool) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        val = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: val.is_bool,
                    text: raw smt_app3("ite", conds.items[k => int64].text, gk.text, val.text),
                    syms: raw syms_union(conds.items[k => int64].syms, raw syms_union(gk.syms, val.syms)) };
    }
    if (!have) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass val;
};

// Does a block's last statement `give`? The shape a pick expression's arm
// takes when its value is the arm's own (L-9).
func:block_ends_in_give = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(body)) { pass false; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, body);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt) { pass true; }
    if (s.kind != StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { pass false; }
    int32:n = raw stmt_list_count(s);
    if (n == 0i32) { pass false; }
    StmtNode:last = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), n - 1i32) });
    pass (last.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt);
};

// Does every statement of a block BEFORE its trailing `give` fall through?
// Then the arm completes with that give's value (L-9).
func:block_reaches_last = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body) never fails {
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, body);
    if (s.kind != StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { pass true; }
    int32:n = raw stmt_list_count(s);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...(n - 1i32)) {
        StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
        if (!(raw stmt_falls_through(e, ch, 64i32))) { pass false; }
    }
    pass true;
};

// A `give` anywhere in a block other than as its last statement -- nested in
// an `if`, a loop, a pick statement -- leaves the arm from inside a
// construct, which the merge does not follow (L-9).
func:stmt_has_nested_give = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(body)) { pass false; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, body);
    if (s.kind != StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, body, fuel)); }
    int32:n = raw stmt_list_count(s);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
        StmtNode:c = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, ch);
        if ((i == (n - 1i32)) && (c.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt)) { continue; }
        if (raw stmt_has_give(e, ch, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

func:stmt_has_give = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass false; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt) { pass true; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
            if (raw stmt_has_give(e, ch, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_then(s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_else(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt)   { pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        if (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            if (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw arm_body(arm), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index }, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    pass false;
};

// THE MERGE OF THE ARMS' VERSIONS (L-8). Over the bindings that existed
// before the construct: the arms that complete contribute their end
// versions; a binding they agree on keeps that version; one they differ on
// gets a new version `(ite c_1 v_1 (ite c_2 v_2 ... v_n))` -- the last
// completing arm the default -- when `mergeable` (every condition a term)
// and every contributing version is named, else a fresh opaque version. One
// completing arm: its versions are adopted and its condition is a fact of
// the parent (the others never fall through). None: nothing after is
// reachable, and nothing is said.
func:merge_arms = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<Term>:conds, List<List<int32>>:snaps, List<bool>:fts,
                      List<int32>:pre, bool:mergeable) never fails {
    int64:arms = fts.count;
    int64:completing = 0i64;
    int64:only = 0i64 - 1i64;
    for (int64:i in 0i64...arms) {
        if (fts.items[i]) { completing = completing + 1i64; only = i; }
    }
    if (completing == 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    if (completing == 1i64) {
        drop adopt_versions(e, snaps.items[only]);
        if (mergeable && conds.items[only].ok) { drop hyp_push(e, conds.items[only].text, conds.items[only].syms); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    int64:n = pre.count;
    if (e.binds.count < n) { n = e.binds.count; }
    for (int64:i2 in 0i64...arms) { if (snaps.items[i2].count < n) { n = snaps.items[i2].count; } }
    for (int64:b in 0i64...n) {
        bool:same = true;
        int32:first = 0i32 - 1i32;
        bool:seen = false;
        bool:named = true;
        for (int64:a in 0i64...arms) {
            if (!fts.items[a]) { continue; }
            int32:v = snaps.items[a].items[b];
            if (v < 0i32) { named = false; }
            if (!seen) { first = v; seen = true; }
            else { if (v != first) { same = false; } }
        }
        if (same) { e.binds.items[b].sym = first; continue; }
        int32:name = e.binds.items[b].name;
        if (!(mergeable && named)) {
            List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop list_push(@one, name);
            drop invalidate(e, one);
            continue;
        }
        // The chain from the last completing arm backwards.
        Term:t = raw term_none();
        bool:have = false;
        int64:k = arms;
        bool:broken = false;
        while (k > 0i64) {
            k = k - 1i64;
            if (!fts.items[k]) { continue; }
            int32:vk = snaps.items[k].items[b];
            Term:tk = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: e.syms.items[vk => int64].is_bool, text: raw sym_text(e, vk),
                            syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64) };
            drop list_push(@tk.syms, vk);
            if (!have) { t = move(tk); have = true; continue; }
            if (!conds.items[k].ok) { broken = true; break; }
            t = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: t.is_bool,
                      text: raw smt_app3("ite", conds.items[k].text, tk.text, t.text),
                      syms: raw syms_union(conds.items[k].syms, raw syms_union(tk.syms, t.syms)) };
        }
        if (broken) {
            List<int32>:one2 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop list_push(@one2, name);
            drop invalidate(e, one2);
            continue;
        }
        drop bind_assign(e, name, t);
        drop assert_rule(e, b);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// One arm's PATTERN as a condition on the selector's term (L-3), or
// `term_none`: a wildcard is the negation of the conditions before it when
// every one of them exists (`prior_ok`), and `true` -- no fact -- when it is
// the first arm.
func:pattern_cond = Term(Encoder->:e, PatNode:p, Term:sel, int32:sel_ty, List<Term>:prior, bool:prior_ok) never fails {
    if (!sel.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatValue) {
        Term:v = raw enc_pattern_value(e, raw pat_value(p), sel_ty);
        if (!(v.ok && (v.is_bool == sel.is_bool))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        pass (raw term_app2("=", sel, v, true));
    }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatRange) {
        if (sel.is_bool) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        Term:lo = raw enc_pattern_value(e, raw pat_range_lo(p), sel_ty);
        Term:hi = raw enc_pattern_value(e, raw pat_range_hi(p), sel_ty);
        if (!(lo.ok && hi.ok && (!lo.is_bool) && (!hi.is_bool))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        Term:ge = raw term_app2("<=", lo, sel, true);
        Term:lt = raw term_app2("<", sel, hi, true);
        if (raw pat_range_inclusive(p)) { lt = raw term_app2("<=", sel, hi, true); }
        pass (raw term_app2("and", ge, lt, true));
    }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatWildcard) {
        if (!prior_ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (prior.count == 0i64) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
        Term:acc = raw term_none();
        bool:first = true;
        for (int64:i in 0i64...prior.count) {
            if (!prior.items[i].ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
            if (first) { acc = raw term_copy(prior.items[i]); first = false; }
            else { acc = raw term_app2("or", acc, prior.items[i], true); }
        }
        pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", acc.text),
                   syms: raw syms_union(acc.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
    }
    pass (raw term_none());
};

// A PATTERN'S VALUE (L-3): the checker compares a pattern with the selector
// and records no type on the pattern's own literal (a pattern is not an
// expression it types for its own sake), so a literal is encoded here under
// the SELECTOR's type -- the checker made it fit -- and a negated literal
// likewise; anything else, a named constant, goes through `enc_expr`.
func:enc_pattern_value = Term(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, int32:sel_ty) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) {
        if (!(raw is_int(e, sel_ty))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, sel_ty)) { pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(n.payload), false)); }
        pass (raw term_lit(raw u64_decimal(n.payload =>! uint64), false));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBoolLiteral) {
        if (!(raw is_bool(e, sel_ty))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (n.payload != 0i64) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
        pass (raw term_lit("false", true));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUnaryExpr) {
        if ((raw expr_op(n)) == TokenKind.OpMinus) {
            ExprNode:o = raw ast_expr(e.ast, raw expr_operand(n));
            if ((o.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) && (raw is_int(e, sel_ty)) && (o.payload >= 0i64)) {
                pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(0i64 - o.payload), false));
            }
        }
    }
    pass (raw enc_expr(e, id));
};

// Is there a `fall` anywhere under this statement? Conservative in the
// direction that matters: a `fall` found means no arm of the pick gets a
// condition (L-3).
func:stmt_has_fall = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass false; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFallStmt) { pass true; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
            if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, ch, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_then(s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_else(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt)   { pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw arm_body(arm), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index }, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    pass false;
};

// DOES A STATEMENT FALL THROUGH TO WHAT FOLLOWS IT (L-2)? False only for a
// syntactic terminator -- `pass`, `fail`, `return`, `exit`, `trap`, `break`,
// `continue`, `give` -- and for a block holding one, an `if` whose two arms
// hold one each, a `pick` whose every arm does. Everything else falls through
// as far as this walk claims: a loop, a `when`, a `defer`, a call, a `fall`,
// `#unreachable()`. Exact in the direction that matters, because the claim
// "never falls through" becomes a hypothesis after the construct.
func:stmt_falls_through = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass true; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPassStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFailStmt)
        || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtReturnStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExitStmt)
        || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTrapStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBreakStmt)
        || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtContinueStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt)) {
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
            if (!(raw stmt_falls_through(e, ch, fuel - 1i32))) { pass false; }
        }
        pass true;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw stmt_then(s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw stmt_else(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            if (raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw arm_body(arm), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass true;
};

// ADOPT an arm's end versions as the current ones (L-2): the other arm never
// falls through, so what follows sees exactly this arm's state. A limited
// name whose version changed gets its rule re-asserted in this region, as a
// merge's havoc would (1.5.2 L-7).
func:adopt_versions = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<int32>:vers) never fails {
    int64:n = vers.count;
    if (e.binds.count < n) { n = e.binds.count; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...n) {
        bool:changed = (e.binds.items[i].sym != vers.items[i]);
        e.binds.items[i].sym = vers.items[i];
        if (changed) { drop assert_rule(e, i); }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:walk_block = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    if (s.kind != StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { drop walk_stmt(e, sid); pass NIL; }
    int64:mark = raw scope_mark(e);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
        drop walk_stmt(e, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) });
    }
    drop scope_release(e, mark);
    pass NIL;
};

pub func:walk_stmt = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { drop walk_block(e, sid); pass NIL; }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
        int32:name = raw stmt_name(s);
        int32:dty = raw subst_emitted_param(e.ctx, raw resolve_type(e.tr, raw stmt_decl_type(s), e.scope));
        ExprId:init = raw stmt_decl_init(e.ast, s);
        Term:t = raw term_none();
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(init))) { t = raw enc_expr(e, init); }
        int32:vrule = raw limit_rule_of(e, raw stmt_decl_limit(e.ast, s));
        drop bind_define(e, name, dty, t, vrule, false);
        // THE FIRST WRITE POINT (1.5.2 step 3, D-251, L-7): after the new
        // version and its definition, the site's obligation -- the rule over
        // the version -- and THEN the rule as a hypothesis, so the goal is
        // never in its own cone. A declaration without an initialiser is not
        // a write point and gets no hypothesis: its vacant value is never
        // read (definite assignment); its first assignment is the write.
        if ((vrule != 0i32) && (!(raw expr_is_none(init)))) {
            drop after_write(e, name, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        TokenKind:op = raw stmt_op(s);
        ExprId:target = raw stmt_target(s);
        ExprNode:tn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, target);
        Term:rhs = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_assigned(s));
        if (tn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            // A field, element or pointee write: its own subexpressions are
            // sites; no local symbol changes (an address-taken local is never
            // defined, so a write through a pointer invalidates nothing here).
            drop walk_children(e, tn);
            if ((op == TokenKind.OpSlashAssign) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercentAssign)) {
                int32:pt = raw ty_of(e, target);
                if (raw is_int(e, pt)) {
                    Term:cur = raw term_opaque(e, pt);
                    drop record_division(e, pt, cur, rhs, target.index, s.span);
                }
            }
            // THE SECOND WRITE POINT through a field or element (D-251): the
            // ROOT's rule over the root's whole value -- `unencoded` while the
            // root's type is outside the fragment (L-6), and no hypothesis
            // (the root has no symbol to assert over).
            drop after_write(e, raw limited_root_name(e, target), raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span);
            pass NIL;
        }
        int32:name = tn.payload =>! int32;
        drop assign_ident(e, s, op, target, name, rhs);
        // THE SECOND WRITE POINT (D-251, L-7), AFTER the new version: the
        // site's obligation, then the rule as a hypothesis.
        drop after_write(e, name, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        // THE CONDITION IS A FACT IN THE ARM IT GUARDS (L-1): `c` in the
        // then-region, `(not c)` in the else-region; nothing when it is
        // outside the fragment. Encoded LOUD in the parent: it runs on every
        // path.
        Term:c = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_cond(s));
        bool:has_c = c.ok && c.is_bool;
        Term:nc = raw term_none();
        if (has_c) {
            nc = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", c.text),
                       syms: raw syms_union(c.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        StmtId:then_s = raw stmt_then(s);
        StmtId:else_s = raw stmt_else(s);
        List<int32>:snap = raw snapshot(e);
        if (has_c) { drop region_enter_cond(e, c); drop hyp_push(e, c.text, c.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        drop walk_block(e, then_s);
        drop region_leave(e);
        List<int32>:snap_then = raw snapshot(e);
        drop restore(e, snap);
        if (has_c) { drop region_enter_cond(e, nc); drop hyp_push(e, nc.text, nc.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        drop walk_block(e, else_s);
        drop region_leave(e);
        List<int32>:snap_else = raw snapshot(e);
        drop restore(e, snap);
        // AFTER THE `if` (L-2, L-8): the two arms merge -- an arm that never
        // falls through contributes nothing; a binding the arms left at
        // different versions is `(ite c then else)` when both are named and
        // the condition has a term, a havoc otherwise.
        List<Term>:conds = raw list_init::<Term>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@conds, raw term_copy(c));
        drop list_push(@conds, raw term_copy(nc));
        List<List<int32>>:snaps = raw list_init::<List<int32>>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@snaps, move(snap_then));
        drop list_push(@snaps, move(snap_else));
        List<bool>:fts = raw list_init::<bool>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@fts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, then_s, 64i32));
        drop list_push(@fts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, else_s, 64i32));
        drop merge_arms(e, conds, snaps, fts, snap, has_c);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) {
        drop walk_loop(e, sid, raw stmt_while_invariant(e.ast, s), raw stmt_body(e.ast, s),
                       raw stmt_cond(s), raw stmt_label(s), raw counter_none());
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) {
        // A RANGE `for` (L-12): the bounds are the range node's two operands
        // (sites, encoded once here), captured at entry (D-234), the limit
        // exclusive (`..` adds one); the binding's entry version is the low
        // bound, its body version a havoc inside the bounds. Any other
        // iterable: the binding opaque, havoced per body.
        ExprId:iter = raw stmt_for_iter(e.ast, s);
        Counter:ctr = raw counter_none();
        DeclNode:bd = raw ast_decl(e.ast, raw stmt_for_binding(s));
        int32:bt = raw subst_emitted_param(e.ctx, raw resolve_type(e.tr, raw param_type(bd), e.scope));
        ctr.kind = 1i32;
        ctr.name = raw decl_name(bd);
        Term:entry = raw term_none();
        bool:is_range = false;
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(iter))) {
            ExprNode:itn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, iter);
            if (itn.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr) { is_range = true; }
        }
        if (is_range) {
            ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, iter);
            Term:lo = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_lhs(rn));
            Term:hi = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(rn));
            if (rn.payload == 1i64) {
                if (hi.ok && (!hi.is_bool)) { hi = raw term_app2("+", hi, raw term_lit("1", false), false); }
                else { hi = raw term_none(); }
            }
            ctr.ranged = true;
            ctr.start = raw term_capture(e, bt, lo);
            ctr.limit = raw term_capture(e, bt, hi);
            ctr.step = raw term_lit("1", false);
            ctr.asc = raw term_lit("true", true);
            entry = raw term_copy(ctr.start);
        } else {
            Term:it = raw enc_expr(e, iter);
        }
        int64:mark = raw scope_mark(e);
        drop bind_define(e, raw decl_name(bd), bt, entry, 0i32, false);
        drop walk_loop(e, sid, raw stmt_for_invariant(e.ast, s), raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s),
                       ExprId{ index: 0i32 }, raw stmt_label(s), ctr);
        drop scope_release(e, mark);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        // THE HEAD (L-11, L-13): `loop(start, limit, step)` or `till(limit,
        // step)` -- each argument a site, encoded once; the start (`0` for
        // `till`), the limit and the step captured; the direction `asc =
        // start < limit` as the emitter computes it once. A COMPUTED step's
        // positivity is the `loop-step` row (S-46), its compare the guard,
        // and `step > 0` is then a fact of every continuing execution (the
        // guard trapped otherwise); a literal step is the checker's (TYPE-068)
        // -- no row, no guard -- and positive by construction.
        int32:argc = raw stmt_counted_argc(e.ast, s);
        int32:i64t = raw tt_int(e.types, 64i32, true);
        Counter:ctr = raw counter_none();
        ctr.kind = 2i32;
        List<Term>:args = raw list_init::<Term>(4i64);
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...argc) {
            drop list_push(@args, raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_counted_arg(e.ast, s, ai)));
        }
        Term:st = raw term_lit("0", false);
        Term:li = raw term_none();
        Term:sp = raw term_none();
        if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt) {
            if (argc == 2i32) { li = raw term_copy(args.items[0i64]); sp = raw term_copy(args.items[1i64]); }
        } else {
            if (argc == 3i32) {
                st = raw term_copy(args.items[0i64]);
                li = raw term_copy(args.items[1i64]);
                sp = raw term_copy(args.items[2i64]);
            }
        }
        ctr.start = raw term_capture(e, i64t, st);
        ctr.limit = raw term_capture(e, i64t, li);
        ctr.step = raw term_capture(e, i64t, sp);
        if (ctr.start.ok && ctr.limit.ok) { ctr.asc = raw term_app2("<", ctr.start, ctr.limit, true); }
        StepLit:sl = raw counted_step_literal(e.ast, s);
        if (sl.is_lit) {
            if (argc >= 1i32) {
                ExprNode:sx = raw ast_expr(e.ast, raw stmt_counted_arg(e.ast, s, argc - 1i32));
                if (sx.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) { ctr.lit_step = sx.payload; }
            }
        } else {
            if (ctr.step.ok) {
                Term:pos = raw term_app2(">", ctr.step, raw term_lit("0", false), true);
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_LOOP_STEP(), pos.text, pos.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true,
                               raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
                drop hyp_push(e, pos.text, pos.syms);
            } else {
                List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_LOOP_STEP(), "", none, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                               raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
            }
        }
        if (sl.is_lit && ctr.step.ok) {
            Term:pos2 = raw term_app2(">", ctr.step, raw term_lit("0", false), true);
            drop hyp_push(e, pos2.text, pos2.syms);
        }
        drop walk_loop(e, sid, raw stmt_counted_invariant(e.ast, s), raw stmt_counted_body(s),
                       ExprId{ index: 0i32 }, raw stmt_label(s), ctr);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        // The loop half through `walk_loop`; then `then` and `end` as the two
        // arms of "did the body run" (L-5, D-027): the body ran at least once
        // exactly when the condition held at the FIRST head visit, over the
        // pre-loop versions. `then` knows that; `end` knows its negation and
        // that the loop changed nothing -- every name the body havoced equals
        // its pre-loop version. The condition over the pre-loop versions is
        // encoded QUIET (its sites are the body region's, once).
        List<int32>:ka = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
        drop collect_assigned(e, sid, @ka);
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:cpre = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_cond(s));
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        bool:has_pre = cpre.ok && cpre.is_bool;
        List<int32>:snap_pre = raw snapshot(e);
        drop walk_loop(e, sid, raw stmt_when_invariant(e.ast, s), raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s),
                       raw stmt_cond(s), raw stmt_label(s), raw counter_none());
        List<int32>:snap_post = raw snapshot(e);
        Term:npre = raw term_none();
        if (has_pre) {
            npre = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", cpre.text),
                         syms: raw syms_union(cpre.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        if (has_pre) { drop region_enter_cond(e, cpre); drop hyp_push(e, cpre.text, cpre.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        drop walk_block(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s));
        drop region_leave(e);
        List<int32>:snap_then = raw snapshot(e);
        drop restore(e, snap_post);
        if (has_pre) { drop region_enter_cond(e, npre); drop hyp_push(e, npre.text, npre.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        int64:np = snap_post.count;
        if (snap_pre.count < np) { np = snap_pre.count; }
        for (int64:bi in 0i64...np) {
            int32:post = snap_post.items[bi];
            int32:pre = snap_pre.items[bi];
            if ((post != pre) && (post >= 0i32) && (pre >= 0i32)) {
                List<int32>:two = raw list_init::<int32>(2i64);
                drop list_push(@two, post);
                drop list_push(@two, pre);
                drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", raw sym_text(e, post), raw sym_text(e, pre)), two);
            }
        }
        drop walk_block(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s));
        drop region_leave(e);
        List<int32>:snap_end = raw snapshot(e);
        drop restore(e, snap_post);
        // THE MERGE (L-8): `then` and `end` are the two arms of "did the body
        // run", the body's own names already havoced by the loop.
        List<Term>:wconds = raw list_init::<Term>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@wconds, raw term_copy(cpre));
        drop list_push(@wconds, raw term_copy(npre));
        List<List<int32>>:wsnaps = raw list_init::<List<int32>>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@wsnaps, move(snap_then));
        drop list_push(@wsnaps, move(snap_end));
        List<bool>:wfts = raw list_init::<bool>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@wfts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), 64i32));
        drop list_push(@wfts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), 64i32));
        drop merge_arms(e, wconds, wsnaps, wfts, snap_post, has_pre);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        Term:sel = raw enc_expr(e, raw pick_selector(s));
        Term:pv = raw walk_pick_arms(e, raw pick_arm_start(s), raw pick_arm_count(s), sel, raw ty_of(e, raw pick_selector(s)), false);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        // Runs at an exit the straight line does not see: every name opaque
        // while it is walked, the outer state restored after.
        List<int32>:snap = raw snapshot(e);
        drop region_enter(e);
        drop invalidate_all(e);
        drop walk_block(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index });
        drop region_leave(e);
        drop restore(e, snap);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt) {
        // THE ARM'S VALUE (L-9): remembered for the pick expression's chain.
        e.last_give = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_expr(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (raw stmt_carries_expr(s.kind)) {
        Term:x = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_expr(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPassStmt) {
        ExprId:pv = raw stmt_operand(s);
        Term:v = raw enc_expr(e, pv);
        drop record_seam(e, sid, s.span, v, raw ty_of(e, pv), !(raw expr_is_none(pv)));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtReturnStmt) {
        // THE LONG FORM (L-12): `return Result{ value: v }` is a success when
        // its error field is absent or the literal 0; the value is `result`.
        ExprId:ro = raw stmt_operand(s);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(ro))) {
            ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, ro);
            if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprResultLiteralExpr) {
                Term:rv = raw term_none();
                bool:has_v = (rn.a != 0i32);
                int32:vty = 0i32;
                if (has_v) { rv = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: rn.a }); vty = raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: rn.a }); }
                bool:success = true;
                if (rn.b != 0i32) {
                    Term:re = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: rn.b });
                    success = false;
                    if (re.ok) { if (string_equals(re.text, "0")) { success = true; } }
                }
                if (success) { drop record_seam(e, sid, s.span, rv, vty, has_v); }
                pass NIL;
            }
        }
        Term:rt = raw enc_expr(e, ro);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExitStmt) {
        ExprId:xo = raw stmt_operand(s);
        Term:xv = raw enc_expr(e, xo);
        // `failsafe`'s POSTCONDITION (L-14, D-267): the code is positive.
        if (e.is_failsafe) {
            if (!xv.ok) { xv = raw term_opaque(e, raw ty_of(e, xo)); }
            if (xv.ok && (!xv.is_bool)) {
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_FAILSAFE_POST(), raw smt_app2(">", xv.text, "0"), xv.syms,
                               raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true, raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
            } else {
                List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_FAILSAFE_POST(), "", none, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                               raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
            }
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFailStmt) {
        Term:fv = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_operand(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtContinueStmt) {
        // A HEAD VISIT (L-8): the invariant of the loop this re-enters holds
        // here -- a preservation row keyed at the `continue`.
        int64:fr = raw loop_frame(e, raw stmt_label(s));
        if (fr >= 0i64) {
            VerifyId:civ = VerifyId{ index: e.loop_invs.items[fr] };
            int32:cnc = raw invariant_clauses(e, civ);
            if (cnc > 0i32) {
                // THE HEAD SEES THE INCREMENTED COUNTER (L-11, L-12): a
                // `continue` re-enters at the increment.
                int32:ck = e.loop_ckind.items[fr];
                if (ck != 0i32) {
                    drop counter_advance(e, ck, e.loop_cname.items[fr], raw term_copy(e.loop_cstep.items[fr]),
                                         raw term_copy(e.loop_casc.items[fr]), e.loop_cdollar.items[fr]);
                }
                e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
                Term:cg = raw invariant_conj(e, civ, false);
                e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
                if (cg.ok) {
                    drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), cg.text, cg.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true,
                                   raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.loop_sids.items[fr], cnc);
                } else {
                    List<int32>:cnone = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                    drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), "", cnone, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                                   raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.loop_sids.items[fr], cnc);
                }
            }
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    // break, fall, and anything unclassified: no sites, no definitions.
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the entry: one function instance ------------------------------------------------------

// Parameters are the first bindings; the escaped set is collected before the
// body is walked, since an address taken late in the body still aliases the
// name from its first definition.
pub func:enc_param = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, int32:ty, int32:rule,
                         int32:decl_index) never fails {
    drop bind_define(e, name, ty, raw term_none(), rule, false);
    // THE THIRD WRITE POINT (1.5.2 step 2, D-251): a limited parameter's
    // check at the callee's entry is a row -- unencoded until step 3.
    if (rule != 0i32) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: decl_index });
        // THE ENTRY WRITE POINT (D-251, L-7): the obligation over the
        // parameter's opaque first version -- `open` unless the type implies
        // the rule -- then the rule as the hypothesis every later read has.
        drop after_write(e, name, raw SITE_DECL(), decl_index, pd.span);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A `Rules` body's clause, walked for its own sites (1.5.2 step 2): the
// predicate function is an instance like any other (P-3).
pub func:enc_clause = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:clause) never fails {
    Term:t = raw enc_expr(e, clause);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE ESCAPE SET FIRST (DEF-14): computed over the whole body BEFORE the
// parameters are bound, so an address-taken parameter is unnamed from its
// first read. 1.5.0 collected it inside `enc_body`, after `enc_param` had
// already given every parameter a stable symbol -- the same hole one line
// earlier.
pub func:enc_prepare = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body) never fails {
    drop collect_escaped(e, body);
    pass NIL;
};

pub func:enc_body = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body) never fails {
    drop walk_block(e, body);
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the cone and the hash (P-4) -----------------------------------------------------------

func:has_sym = bool(List<int32>:l, int32:s) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...l.count) { if (l.items[i] == s) { pass true; } }
    pass false;
};

func:sym_sort = string(Encoder->:e, int32:idx) never fails {
    if (e.syms.items[idx => int64].is_bool) { pass "Bool"; }
    pass "Int";
};

// `(declare-const |x.1| Int)`, or for an uninterpreted function (L-3)
// `(declare-fun |uf.f.7| (Int Int) Int)`.
func:sym_declaration = string(Encoder->:e, int32:idx) never fails {
    string:d = "(declare-const ";
    if (e.syms.items[idx => int64].sorts.len > 0i64) { d = "(declare-fun "; }
    d = string_concat(d, raw sym_text(e, idx));
    d = string_concat(d, " ");
    if (e.syms.items[idx => int64].sorts.len > 0i64) {
        d = string_concat(d, string_from_bytes(e.syms.items[idx => int64].sorts.ptr,
                                               e.syms.items[idx => int64].sorts.len));
        d = string_concat(d, " ");
    }
    d = string_concat(d, raw sym_sort(e, idx));
    pass (string_concat(d, ")"));
};

// Fill every obligation's cone, canonical text and hash.
pub func:enc_finish = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    for (int64:oi in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        if (!e.obls.items[oi].encoded) {
            string:u = string_concat("(unencoded ", raw ok_name(e.obls.items[oi].kind));
            u = string_concat(u, " ");
            u = string_concat(u, int_to_string(e.obls.items[oi].ordinal => int64));
            u = string_concat(u, ")");
            e.obls.items[oi].canon = string_concat(u, "");
            string:hu = string_concat(u, "\n");
            hu = string_concat(hu, e.symbol);
            hu = string_concat(hu, "\n");
            hu = string_concat(hu, raw ok_name(e.obls.items[oi].kind));
            hu = string_concat(hu, "\n");
            e.obls.items[oi].hash = raw sha256_hex(hu);
            continue;
        }
        // The relevance closure over hypotheses [0, hyps).
        int64:limit_h = e.obls.items[oi].hyps;
        List<int32>:cs = raw list_init::<int32>(8i64);
        for (int64:g in 0i64...e.obls.items[oi].syms.count) {
            if (!(raw has_sym(cs, e.obls.items[oi].syms.items[g]))) { drop list_push(@cs, e.obls.items[oi].syms.items[g]); }
        }
        List<bool>:inc = raw list_init::<bool>(limit_h + 1i64);
        for (int64:h0 in 0i64...limit_h) { drop list_push(@inc, false); }
        bool:grew = true;
        while (grew) {
            grew = false;
            for (int64:h in 0i64...limit_h) {
                if (inc.items[h]) { continue; }
                if (!(raw region_dominates(e, e.hyps.items[h].region, e.obls.items[oi].region))) { continue; }
                bool:touch = false;
                for (int64:q in 0i64...e.hyps.items[h].syms.count) {
                    if (raw has_sym(cs, e.hyps.items[h].syms.items[q])) { touch = true; }
                }
                if (!touch) { continue; }
                inc.items[h] = true;
                grew = true;
                for (int64:q2 in 0i64...e.hyps.items[h].syms.count) {
                    if (!(raw has_sym(cs, e.hyps.items[h].syms.items[q2]))) { drop list_push(@cs, e.hyps.items[h].syms.items[q2]); }
                }
            }
        }
        // Symbols ascending (insertion order of declaration), hypotheses in order.
        List<int32>:sorted = raw list_init::<int32>(cs.count + 1i64);
        for (int64:si in 0i64...e.syms.count) {
            if (raw has_sym(cs, si =>! int32)) { drop list_push(@sorted, si =>! int32); }
        }
        List<int32>:hl = raw list_init::<int32>(8i64);
        for (int64:h2 in 0i64...limit_h) { if (inc.items[h2]) { drop list_push(@hl, h2 =>! int32); } }
        SmtBuf:b = raw smtbuf_init();
        for (int64:s2 in 0i64...sorted.count) {
            drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw sym_declaration(e, sorted.items[s2]));
        }
        for (int64:h3 in 0i64...hl.count) {
            drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw smt_app1("assert", string_concat(e.hyps.items[hl.items[h3] => int64].text, "")));
        }
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw smt_app1("assert", raw smt_app1("not", string_concat(e.obls.items[oi].goal, ""))));
        string:canon = raw smtbuf_text(move(b));
        string:hin = string_concat(canon, e.symbol);
        hin = string_concat(hin, "\n");
        hin = string_concat(hin, raw ok_name(e.obls.items[oi].kind));
        hin = string_concat(hin, "\n");
        e.obls.items[oi].hash = raw sha256_hex(hin);
        e.obls.items[oi].canon = move(canon);
        e.obls.items[oi].cone_syms = move(sorted);
        e.obls.items[oi].cone_hyps = move(hl);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// The `--elide` reader marks rows whose hash the manifest lists as discharged.
pub func:enc_mark_discharged = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<string>:hashes) never fails {
    for (int64:oi in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        for (int64:h in 0i64...hashes.count) {
            if (string_equals(e.obls.items[oi].hash, hashes.items[h])) { e.obls.items[oi].discharged = true; }
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Is the site (an ExprId index) of kind `kind` discharged? The emitter's question.
pub func:enc_site_discharged = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:space, int32:site, int32:kind) never fails {
    for (int64:oi in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        if ((e.obls.items[oi].site == site) && (e.obls.items[oi].kind == kind)) {
            if (e.obls.items[oi].space == space) { pass e.obls.items[oi].discharged; }
        }
    }
    pass false;
};

// --- the solver file for one function ------------------------------------------------------

// The header comment, the logic, the definitions, every declaration at the
// base level, then one push/assert/check-sat/pop per obligation over its cone
// (P-6, P-7, P-16, P-17). Unencoded rows take no query.
pub func:enc_file_text = string(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    SmtBuf:b = raw smtbuf_init();
    drop smtbuf_line(@b, string_concat("; ", e.symbol));
    int64:checks = 0i64;
    for (int64:oi in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        string:c = string_concat("; o", int_to_string(oi + 1i64));
        c = string_concat(c, " ");
        c = string_concat(c, raw ok_name(e.obls.items[oi].kind));
        c = string_concat(c, " ");
        c = string_concat(c, e.obls.items[oi].hash);
        c = string_concat(c, " ");
        c = string_concat(c, int_to_string(e.obls.items[oi].line => int64));
        c = string_concat(c, ":");
        c = string_concat(c, int_to_string(e.obls.items[oi].col => int64));
        if (!e.obls.items[oi].encoded) { c = string_concat(c, " unencoded"); }
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, c);
        if (e.obls.items[oi].encoded) { checks = checks + 1i64; }
    }
    drop smtbuf_line(@b, string_concat("; checks ", int_to_string(checks)));
    // THE LOGIC: linear or nonlinear integer arithmetic, with uninterpreted
    // functions (L-3) the moment one is declared -- QF_LIA refuses a
    // `declare-fun` of arity above zero.
    bool:has_uf = false;
    for (int64:ui in 0i64...e.syms.count) { if (e.syms.items[ui].sorts.len > 0i64) { has_uf = true; } }
    if (e.nonlinear) {
        if (has_uf) { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic QF_UFNIA)"); }
        else { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic QF_NIA)"); }
    } else {
        if (has_uf) { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic QF_UFLIA)"); }
        else { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic QF_LIA)"); }
    }
    if (e.uses_sdiv) {
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(define-fun npk_sdiv ((a Int) (b Int)) Int (ite (>= a 0) (ite (>= b 0) (div a b) (- (div a (- b)))) (ite (>= b 0) (- (div (- a) b)) (div (- a) (- b)))))");
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(define-fun npk_srem ((a Int) (b Int)) Int (- a (* b (npk_sdiv a b))))");
    }
    for (int64:si in 0i64...e.syms.count) {
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw sym_declaration(e, si =>! int32));
    }
    for (int64:oi2 in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        if (!e.obls.items[oi2].encoded) { continue; }
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(push)");
        for (int64:h in 0i64...e.obls.items[oi2].cone_hyps.count) {
            int32:hi = e.obls.items[oi2].cone_hyps.items[h];
            string:named = string_concat("(! ", e.hyps.items[hi => int64].text);
            named = string_concat(named, " :named h");
            named = string_concat(named, int_to_string(hi => int64));
            named = string_concat(named, ")");
            drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw smt_app1("assert", named));
        }
        string:goal = string_concat("(! ", raw smt_app1("not", string_concat(e.obls.items[oi2].goal, "")));
        goal = string_concat(goal, " :named o");
        goal = string_concat(goal, int_to_string(oi2 + 1i64));
        goal = string_concat(goal, ")");
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw smt_app1("assert", goal));
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(check-sat)");
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(pop)");
    }
    pass (raw smtbuf_text(move(b)));
};
